hadiths[394]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1201","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man being supported between his two sons. He said: What is this? They said: He vowed to walk to the House. He said: Allah Almighty is in no need of this one's tormenting himself. Then he commanded him, so he rode."
"1202","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, that Umm Sulaym took a dagger on the day of Hunayn. Abu Talhah said: O Messenger of Allah, here is Umm Sulaym with a dagger. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I took it so that if any of the polytheists comes near me, I shall rip open his belly with it. Kill the freed captives; strike their necks; they were defeated because of you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said: Allah Almighty has sufficed and done well."
"1203","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a woman weeping over a child of hers. He said to her: Fear Allah and be patient. She said: What do you care about my calamity? When he left, it was said to her: He is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She was seized as though by death. She came to his door and found no doorkeepers upon it. She said: I did not recognize you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Patience is only at the first shock - or he said: at the first of the shock."
"1204","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said on the day of Uhud while wiping blood from his face: How can a people prosper when they have wounded their prophet, broken his front tooth, and bloodied his face? Then Allah Almighty revealed: You have no part in the matter, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers."
"1205","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi and Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I came upon Musa on the night I was taken by night, by the red dune, while he was standing praying in his grave."
"1206","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When Zaynab's waiting period ended, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Zayd: Go and mention me to her. He said: So Zayd went to her, and behold she was leavening her dough. He said: When I saw her, I could not look at her because of her greatness in my heart, when I knew that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had proposed to her. So I stepped back on my heels and turned my back to her. Then I said: O Zaynab, receive glad tidings; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has sent mentioning you. She said: I shall do nothing until I consult my Lord. So she stood to her place of prayer. He said: And the Quran was revealed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came until he entered upon her without permission. Anas said: You saw us when she was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he fed us bread and meat over her until the day stretched, and the people left while a group remained conversing after the food. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, and I followed him, and he began to visit his wives, greeting them, and they said: How did you find your wife, O Messenger of Allah? Anas said: I do not know whether I informed him that the people had left or he was informed. He proceeded until he reached the house and found them gone, so he entered, and I went to enter with him, but he drew the curtain between me and him. He said: And the veil was revealed. He said: And the people were admonished with what they were admonished with: Do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless permission is given to you, up to His saying: And Allah is not shy of the truth."
"1207","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: Concerning Zaynab bint Jahsh was revealed: And you conceal within yourself what Allah will disclose. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her, and he did not give a wedding feast for any of his wives as he gave for her; he slaughtered a sheep."
"1208","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, that eighty men descended upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions from Mount al-Tan'im at the dawn prayer, intending to kill him. They were seized all together, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed them. Then Allah revealed: And it is He who withheld their hands from you and your hands from them in the valley of Makkah, after He gave you victory over them."
"1209","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to me, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: When this verse was revealed: O you who believe, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet, up to His saying: While you perceive not - and Thabit ibn Qays ibn al-Shammas had a loud voice - he said: I am the one who used to raise my voice over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); my deeds are nullified; I am of the people of the Fire. So he sat among his family, grieved. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed him, so some of the people went to him and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has missed you; what is the matter with you? He said: I am the one who used to raise my voice above the voice of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and speak loudly to him; my deeds are nullified; I am of the people of the Fire. They came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of what he said. He said: No; rather he is of the people of Paradise. Anas said: We used to see him walking among us while we knew he was of the people of Paradise. When the day of al-Yamamah came - Anas said: and I was among them - he said: There was among us some exposure, so Thabit ibn Qays came, having perfumed himself and worn his shroud, and said: Evil is what you accustom your peers to. Then he fought them until he was killed, may Allah have mercy on him."
"1210","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Frequented House is in the fourth heaven; seventy thousand angels enter it every day, then they do not return to it until the Hour is established."
"1211","Ali ibn Asim narrated to me, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: When the polytheists were defeated, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and stood. Then he commanded concerning Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, so he was dragged and cast into the pit. Then he commanded concerning Utbah ibn Rabi'ah, so he was dragged and cast into the pit. Then he commanded concerning Shaybah ibn Rabi'ah, so he was dragged and cast into the pit. Then he commanded concerning Umayyah ibn Khalaf, so he was dragged and cast into the pit, while Abu Hudhayfah ibn Utbah was standing beside the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not notice him. When he saw his father being dragged until cast into the pit, his face changed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to him, and when he saw his face changed, he said: O Abu Hudhayfah, it is as though what we did with Utbah distressed you. He said: O Messenger of Allah, why should I not be a believer in Allah and His Messenger? But there was no one among the people who resembled Utbah in intellect and in nobility, so I hoped Allah Almighty would guide him to Islam. When I saw his slain state, that grieved me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke good to him. In the depth of the night, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, and the people heard him calling in the depth of the night: O Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, and O Utbah ibn Rabi'ah, and O Shaybah ibn Rabi'ah, and O Umayyah ibn Khalaf, have you found what your Lord promised you true? For I have found what my Lord promised me true. He said: The people called to him: O Messenger of Allah, do you call out to a people who have decayed? He said: By Allah, you are not more hearing of what I say than they, but they are unable to answer."
"1212","Ubayd al-Attar narrated to me, Sinan ibn Harun al-Burjumi narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas, who said: Umm Habibah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: O Messenger of Allah, a woman among us has two husbands in this world, then she dies and enters Paradise, she and her two husbands; to which of them will she belong, the first or the last? He said: She will choose the better of the two in character, as he was with her in this world, and he will be her husband in Paradise. O Umm Habibah, good character has carried away the good of this world and the good of the Hereafter."
"1213","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): People from among my Companions will come to me at the Basin, until when I see them and recognize them, they are snatched away before reaching me. So I shall say: O Lord, my companions, my companions. Then it will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"1214","Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) counseled, while his tongue could hardly move, saying: Prayer, and what your right hands possess."
"1215","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, saying: Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman, freedman of Ibn Abbas, narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah Almighty created the earth, it began to sway, so He created the mountains and cast them upon it, and it settled. The angels marveled at the strength of the mountains and said: O Lord, is there anything of Your creation stronger than the mountains? He said: Yes, iron. They said: O Lord, is there anything of Your creation stronger than iron? He said: Yes, fire. They said: O Lord, is there anything of Your creation stronger than fire? He said: Yes, water. They said: O Lord, is there anything of Your creation stronger than water? He said: Yes, wind. They said: O Lord, is there anything of Your creation stronger than wind? He said: Yes, the man who gives charity with his right hand, concealing it from his left."
"1216","Abu al-Walid and Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to me, both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the Hour is established while a sapling is in the hand of one of you, then if he is able not to rise until he plants it, let him plant it."
"1217","Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to me, from Fudayl ibn Iyad, from Hisham, from Hanzalah al-Sadusi, from Anas, who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, should one of us bow to another when we meet? He said: No. We said: Should one of us embrace another? He said: No. We said: Should one of us shake hands with another? He said: Yes."
"1218","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Anas ibn Malik, that Hilal ibn Umayyah accused his wife with Sharik ibn Sahma'. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Watch her; if she brings him white and straight-haired, then he is Hilal ibn Umayyah's, and if she brings him dark-eyed, curly-haired, thin in the shanks, then he is Sharik ibn Sahma's. She brought him dark-eyed, curly-haired, thin in the shanks."
"1219","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Anas, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shaved, he began with the right side of his head, then gave it to Abu Talhah, then shaved the left side, and divided it among the people."
"1220","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, Mu'an ibn Rifa'ah al-Salami informed us, from Abu Khalaf al-A'ma, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My ummah will never unite upon misguidance; when you see disagreement, hold to the great majority."
"1221","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A bulky man of the Ansar could not pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: O Messenger of Allah, I am unable to pray with you, so show me how you pray so that I may pray as you pray. He said: He prepared food for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then invited him to his house. He said: He sprinkled water on the edge of a mat for the Messenger of Allah, then prayed two rak'ahs. A man of Banu al-Jarud among the people of Basrah said to Anas ibn Malik: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray Duha? He said: I never saw him pray it before that day."
"1222","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw, on the night I was taken by night, men whose lips were being clipped with scissors of fire. I said to Jibril: Who are these? He said: These are preachers of your ummah who command people to righteousness and forget themselves, while they recite the Book; will they not understand?"
"1223","Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pass by the door of Fatimah for six months when he went out for the dawn prayer, saying: Prayer, O people of the house: Allah only intends to remove defilement from you, O people of the house, and to purify you thoroughly."
"1224","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Zayd informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: Today I recognize sins that are finer in your eyes than a hair; we used to count them in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the major sins."
"1225","Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first to be clothed with a garment of Fire is Iblis; he places it upon his eyebrow and drags it behind him, saying: O my ruin! And his offspring behind him say: O our ruin! Then it is said: Do not call today for one ruin, but call for many ruins."
"1226","Yazid ibn Abi Hakim narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, who said: I asked Anas about al-Safa and al-Marwah. He said: They were among the rites of ignorance, so when Islam came, we held back from them. Then Allah Almighty revealed: Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah; whoever performs Hajj to the House or Umrah, there is no blame upon him to go round them. He said: They are voluntary, and whoever volunteers good, then Allah is Appreciative, Knowing."
"1227","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Zilal informed us, saying: I came upon Anas ibn Malik, and he said to me: Come near; when did your sight go? I said: When I was two years old, as my family claims. He said: Shall I not give you glad tidings with which your eye will be cooled? I said: Yes indeed. He said: Ibn Umm Maktum passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted him, then went on. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty says: For one whose two precious things I take, I have no reward with Me but Paradise."
"1228","Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Bakr ibn Ubaydullah ibn Anas, from his grandfather Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty said: By My might, I do not take the two precious things - or the two beloved things - of a servant, and he is patient and content with My decree, then I am content for him with a reward less than Paradise."
"1229","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Shu'bah informed us, from Muslim al-A'war, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit the sick, attend funerals, accept the invitation of a slave, and ride the donkey; and I saw him on the day of Khaybar upon a donkey whose bridle was of palm fiber."
"1230","Ja'far ibn Awn informed us, Muslim al-A'war informed us, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on the day of Khaybar and the day of al-Nadir, was upon a donkey with a packsaddle bridled with a rope of palm fiber."
"1231","Ja'far ibn Awn informed us, Muslim al-Mulai informed us, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Zuhr when the sun declined, and pray Asr while the sun was white and clear, and pray Maghrib when it set, and delay Isha, saying: Be watchful, and do not sleep; and pray Fajr when the light covered the sky."
"1232","Habban ibn Hilal narrated to me, Khalid al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muslim al-A'war narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a Coptic shirt, short in length and short in sleeves."
"1233","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Rib'i ibn Abdullah ibn al-Jarud informed us, saying: Amr ibn Abi al-Hajjaj narrated to me, from al-Jarud ibn Abi Sabrah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to pray voluntarily upon his mount, he would face the qiblah and pronounce the takbir, then let it go its way, then pray upon his mount whichever direction it turned with him."
"1234","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Hisham al-Dastuwai informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke his fast with a people, he would say: The fasting have broken fast with you, the righteous have eaten your food, and the angels have descended upon you."
"1235","Ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Nufay', from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no one, rich or poor, except that on the Day of Resurrection he will wish he had been given only sustenance in this world."
"1236","Ja'far ibn Awn informed us, Usamah ibn Zayd informed us, from Hafs ibn Ubaydullah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Many a disheveled, dusty man in two worn garments, if he swore by Allah, He would fulfill it for him."
"1237","Zakariyya ibn Adi informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Hafs ibn Ubaydullah ibn Anas, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to break his fast with fresh dates before going out on the day of Eid."
"1238","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, that he heard Anas ibn Malik say: Abu Talhah said to Umm Sulaym: I heard the voice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) weak, in which I recognize hunger; do you have anything? She said: Yes. She brought out loaves of barley, then brought out a headcover of hers, wrapped the bread in part of it, tucked it under my arm, and covered me with part of it. Then she sent me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I went with it and found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque with the people. I stood over them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Did Abu Talhah send you? I said: Yes. He said: For food? I said: Yes. He said to those with him: Arise, let us go. I walked ahead of them until I came to Abu Talhah and informed him. Abu Talhah said: O Umm Sulaym, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has come, and we do not have food to suffice them. She said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Abu Talhah went out until he met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came with Abu Talhah accompanying him until they entered. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring forth, O Umm Sulaym, what you have. She brought that bread, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded concerning it, so it was crumbled, and Umm Sulaym squeezed a butter skin of hers over it as condiment. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said over it what Allah willed him to say. Then he said: Admit ten. They were admitted, ate until full, then left. Then he said: Admit ten. They were admitted, ate until full, then left. Then he said: Admit ten, and all the people ate and were full, and the people were seventy or eighty men."
"1239","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madinah, the Abyssinians played out of joy at his arrival; they played with their spears."
"1240","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Umm Sulaym had a son by Abu Talhah. He fell ill, then died, so she covered him with a garment. Abu Talhah came in and said: How is my son this evening? She said: He is calm this evening. He ate supper. Then in part of the night she said: What do you think, if a man lent you something on loan, then took it back from you, would you grieve? He said: No. She said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, lent you your son, and He has taken him. He said: In the morning he went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of her saying. He said: And he had been with her that night. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah bless you both in your night. She gave birth to a boy named Abdullah, and it was mentioned that he was among the best of the people of his time."
"1241","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Obscenity is never in anything except that it disgraces it, and modesty is never in anything except that it adorns it."
"1242","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached to the middle of his ears."
"1243","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I counted on the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his beard only fourteen white hairs."
"1244","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that Usayd ibn Hudayr and another man of the Ansar were conversing with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night concerning a need of theirs, until an hour of the night had passed, on a night of intense darkness. Then they left the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), turning to go, each with a small staff in his hand. The staff of one of them lit up for them both, and they walked in its light until, when the road parted them, the staff of the other lit up for him. Each of them walked in the light of his staff until he reached his family."
"1245","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed marriage on behalf of Julaybib to a woman of the Ansar, to her father. He said: Until I consult her mother. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then yes, in that case. The man went to his wife and mentioned that to her. She said: By Allah, then has the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found none but Julaybib! We have refused her to so-and-so and so-and-so. He said: And the girl was behind her curtain, listening. The man set out to inform the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of that. The girl said: Do you intend to turn back the command of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? If he has approved him for you, then marry her to him. It was as though she removed the doubt from her parents, and they said: She has spoken the truth. Her father went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: If you had approved him, then we have approved him. He said: I have approved him. He said: So he married her to him. Then the people of Madinah were alarmed to war, and Julaybib rode out. They found him slain, with people of the polytheists around him whom he had slain. Anas said: I saw her, and she was among the most spending households in Madinah."
"1246","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: None of you should wish for death because of a harm that has befallen him."
"1247","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not be established upon anyone who says: Allah, Allah."
"1248","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that it reached Safiyyah that Hafsah said: O daughter of a Jew. She wept, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to her while she was weeping. He said: What makes you weep? She said: Hafsah said: I am the daughter of a Jew. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are the daughter of a prophet, and your uncle is a prophet, and you are under a prophet, so with what does she boast over you? Then he said: Fear Allah, O Hafsah."
"1249","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), after the prayer had been established, a man speaking to him about his need, standing between him and the qiblah. He remained standing speaking to him, until I saw some of the people dozing from the length of the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing with him."
"1250","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit and Aban, from Anas, who said: I never prayed, after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a prayer lighter than the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in completeness of bowing and prostration."
"1251","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tend to these rows, for I see you from behind me."
"1252","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes raise his head from the prostration or the bowing and remain between them, until we would say: Has he forgotten?"
"1253","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took from the women, when he pledged them, that they not wail. They said: O Messenger of Allah, women aided us in wailing in ignorance; shall we aid them in Islam? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no aiding in wailing in Islam, nor shighar in Islam, nor slaughtering at graves in Islam, nor jallab, nor janab, and whoever plunders is not of us."
"1254","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah wanted to marry a woman. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Go and look at her, for it is more likely to bring harmony between you. He said: He did so, married her, and mentioned her compatibility."
"1255","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Dubai informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: Umm Sulaym brought me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I was a boy, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, this is Unays, supplicate for him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, increase his wealth and his children, and admit him to Paradise. He said: I have indeed seen two of them, and I hope for the third."
"1256","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar."
"1257","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Dubai informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah for the compensatory Umrah while Ibn Rawahah walked before him saying verses, and Umar said: O Ibn Rawahah, do you recite poetry before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and in the Sanctuary of Allah? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him, for it is swifter upon them than the shooting of arrows."
"1258","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: that the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not go beyond his ears."
"1259","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to me, my father narrated to us, saying: I heard Thabit al-Bunani narrating from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, do not stand until you see me."
"1260","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to me, my father narrated to us, saying: I heard Thabit al-Bunani narrating from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes come down from the pulpit on Friday and a man would meet him and speak to him about his need, so he would stand with him, then enter into the prayer."
"1261","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to me, Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, who said: Anas ibn Malik used to describe to us the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he would stand and pray, and when he raised his head from bowing he would stand so long that we would say: he has forgotten; and when he raised his head from the first prostration he would sit so long that we would say: he has forgotten."
"1262","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Shubah, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would often say: O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and shield us from the punishment of the Fire. Shubah said: I mentioned that to Qatadah, and he said: Anas used to supplicate with this."
"1263","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited all his wives together. Sulayman said: meaning in one night, all of them."
"1264","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They name him Muhammad, then they revile him."
"1265","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man loves another man but cannot do deeds like his. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A person is with the one he loves."
"1266","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray at night in Ramadan, so I came and stood beside him, and another man came and stood as well, until we were a group. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sensed that we were behind him, he shortened his prayer, then entered his lodging and prayed a prayer he did not pray with us. We said to him in the morning: Did you notice us last night? He said: Yes, that is what prompted what I did. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began observing uninterrupted fasting at the end of the month, and some of his Companions began doing the same, so he said: You are not like me. By Allah, if the month were extended for me, I would fast continuously in a manner that would make the extremists abandon their extremism."
"1267","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us when there was no one there but me, my mother, and my maternal aunt Umm Haram. He said: Stand, so that I may pray with you outside the time of a prescribed prayer, and he prayed with us. A man said to Thabit: Where did he place Anas relative to himself? He said: He placed him on his right. Then he supplicated for us, the people of the house, with every good of this world and the Hereafter. My mother said: O Messenger of Allah, your little servant, supplicate to Allah for him. So he supplicated for me with all good, and among the last of what he supplicated was: O Allah, increase his wealth and his children, and bless him therein."
"1268","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to me, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and took his midday rest at our house, and he sweated. My mother brought a bottle and began collecting his sweat in it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke up and said: O Umm Sulaym, what is this that you are doing? She said: This is your sweat; we put it in our perfume, and it is among the finest perfume, from the scent of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Thabit said: Anas ibn Malik said: I never smelled any ambergris or musk more fragrant, nor ever touched anything, brocade, khazz, or silk, softer to the touch than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Thabit said: I said, O Abu Hamzah: Is it as though you still look at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and hear his voice? He said: Yes indeed, by Allah, I hope to meet him on the Day of Resurrection and say: O Messenger of Allah, your little servant. He said: I served him for ten years in Madinah while I was a boy; not every man is as his companion would wish him to be; he never once said to me Uff, nor said to me: Why did you do this, or: Why did you not do this."
"1269","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to me, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: I was running among the boys while they said: Muhammad has come, so I would run and see nothing, then they would say: Muhammad has come, and I would run and see nothing, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came with his companion Abu Bakr al-Siddiq. We were in one of the ruined quarters of Madinah, then they sent a Bedouin man to announce them to the Ansar. About five hundred of the Ansar met them until they reached them, and the Ansar said: Proceed, secure and obeyed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companion came forward among them, and the people of Madinah came out, so much so that the unmarried girls were above the houses watching him, saying: Which one is he, which one is he? He said: We never saw a sight like that day. Anas said: I saw him on the day he entered among us and on the day he passed away, and I never saw two days like them."
"1270","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day until, when I saw that I had finished serving him, I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will take his midday rest. So I went out and found some boys playing, and I stood watching their play. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, greeted them, then called me and sent me on an errand of his, and he was in the shade until I returned to him. I was late for my mother beyond the time I used to come to her, so she said: What kept you? I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on an errand of his. She said: What is it? I said: It is a secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: Guard the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I never told anyone among the people about that errand; had I told anyone, I would have told you."
"1271","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to me, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will come to the gate of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection and ask for it to be opened. The keeper will say: Who are you? I will say: Muhammad. He will say: I was commanded concerning you not to open for anyone before you."
"1272","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to me, Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Busaysah as a scout to see what the caravan of Abu Sufyan had done. He returned when there was no one in the house except me and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — I do not recall whether he excepted some of his wives — and he told him the report. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and spoke, saying: We have an objective to seek, so whoever has his mount present, let him ride with us. Some men began asking his permission regarding their camels kept in the upper part of Madinah, and he said: No, except whoever has his mount present. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions set out until they reached Badr before the polytheists, and the polytheists came. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you advance toward anything until I announce it. The polytheists drew near, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rise toward a Paradise whose breadth is the heavens and the earth. Umayr ibn Humam al-Ansari said: O Messenger of Allah, a Paradise whose breadth is the heavens and the earth? He said: Yes. He said: Bakh, bakh. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What prompts you to say bakh, bakh? He said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, nothing but hope that I will be among its people. He said: Then you are among its people. He took some dates from his quiver and began eating them, then said: If I live until I finish eating these dates of mine, it is indeed a long life. So he threw away the dates he had, then fought them until he was killed, may Allah have mercy on him."
"1273","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the barber was shaving him, and his Companions surrounded him, wanting no hair to fall except into the hand of a man."
"1274","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to me, saying: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to me, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had prayed the dawn prayer, the servants of Madinah would come with their vessels containing water, and no vessel was brought but he dipped his hand in it; they would sometimes come to him on a cold morning and he would dip his hand in it."
"1275","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to me, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked good dreams, and among what he would say was: Has any of you seen a dream? If the man he did not know saw one, he would ask about him, and if he was told something good about him, his dream would please him all the more. A woman came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw in sleep as though I was taken out and admitted to Paradise, and I heard a thud at which Paradise shook, and there were so-and-so the son of so-and-so and so-and-so the son of so-and-so, until she counted twelve men — the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had sent an expedition before that — and they were brought wearing dusty garments with their jugular veins spurting. It was said: Take them to the river al-Baydhakh. They were dipped in it and came out with faces like the moon on the night of full moon. Chairs of gold were brought and they sat on them, and a platter of gold containing unripe dates was brought, and they ate of the dates as they wished; they would not turn it to any side but they ate of whatever fruit they wished. She said: O Messenger of Allah, and I ate with them. Then the bearer of glad tidings came from that expedition and said: O Messenger of Allah, such-and-such happened, and so-and-so and so-and-so were struck, until he counted twelve men. He said: Bring me the woman. She came, and he said: Relate your dream to him. The man said: It is as she said; so-and-so and so-and-so were struck."
"1276","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, who said: We were with Anas when he wrote a document between his family members, and he said: Bear witness, O company of reciters. Thabit said: It is as though I disliked that, so I said: O Abu Hamzah, if only you named them by their names. He said: What harm is there in my calling you reciters? Shall I not narrate to you about your brothers whom we used to call the reciters in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He mentioned that they were seventy. When night covered them, they would go to a place of learning in Madinah and study the Quran there until morning. When morning came, whoever had strength would fetch sweet water and gather firewood, and whoever had means, they would pool together and buy a sheep and prepare it, and by morning that would be hung at the apartments of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When Khubayb was struck, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent them, and they came upon a clan of Banu Sulaym among whom was my uncle Haram. Haram said to their chief: Let me go and inform these people that we do not intend them, so that they let us pass. Haram said to them: We do not intend you, so let us pass. A man met him with a spear and pierced him through with it, and when he felt the spear in his belly he said: Allah is Most Great, I have succeeded, by the Lord of the Kabah. Then they closed in on them and none of them remained. Anas said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grieve over anything as he grieved over them. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whenever he prayed the dawn prayer, raise his hands and supplicate against them. Later, Abu Talhah said to me: What about the killer of Haram? I said: What is with him, may Allah do to him and do. He said: Wait, for he has become Muslim."
"1277","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to me, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: A man invited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he went, and I went with him. Broth containing pumpkin was brought, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began eating that pumpkin and it pleased him. When I saw that, I began putting it before him and did not eat any of it myself. Anas said: I have loved it ever since. Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah said: I narrated this hadith to Sulayman al-Taymi, who said: We never visited Anas ibn Malik in the season of pumpkin but we found it in his food."
"1278","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to me, saying: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: There was a man among us from Banu al-Najjar who had recited al-Baqarah and Al Imran and used to write for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He fled and joined the People of the Book. They honored him and said: This one used to write for Muhammad, and they were impressed by him. It was not long before Allah broke his neck among them. They dug for him and buried him, but by morning the earth had cast him out upon its surface. Then they returned, dug for him and buried him, but by morning the earth had cast him out upon its surface, so they left him cast out."
"1279","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to me, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: Abu Talhah had a son who had a small sparrow he played with, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Umayr, what happened to the little sparrow?"
"1280","Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah informed us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik: that a scribe of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined the polytheists, and they said: This is the scribe of Muhammad; he has chosen your religion, so honor him. He was honored, and it was not long before he died. A grave was dug for him, but the earth threw him out; then a grave was dug for him again, but the earth threw him out, so he was cast in one of those ravines."
"1281","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to me, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, who said: Anas ibn Malik described to us the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then stood and prayed with us. He bowed, then stood upright until some of us thought he had forgotten; then he prostrated, then sat upright until some of us thought he had forgotten, then sat upright."
"1282","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to me, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: I was standing by the pulpit on Friday while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon, when one of the people of the mosque said: O Messenger of Allah, rain has been withheld and livestock have perished, so supplicate to Allah the Mighty and Majestic to give us rain. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands, though we saw no cloud in the sky, and Allah the Exalted brought the clouds together, and it rained heavily upon us until we saw a strong man concerned only with reaching his family. We were rained upon for seven days without ceasing until the next Friday, with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering the sermon, when one of the people said: O Messenger of Allah, houses have collapsed and travel has been cut off; supplicate to Allah to lift it from us. He raised his hands and said: O Allah, around us and not upon us. What was above our heads dispersed as though we were under a canopy; it rained around us while we were not rained upon."
"1283","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: I saw a wedding feast of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which there was neither bread nor meat. Safiyyah had fallen to Dihyah al-Kalbi in his share, and they began praising her to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: We have seen among the captives a woman the like of whom we have never seen among the captives. So he sent to Dihyah and gave him in exchange what pleased him. Then he entrusted her to Umm Sulaym and said: Prepare her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Khaybar until he had put it behind him, then halted and pitched a tent over her, then in the morning said: Whoever has extra provisions, let him bring them to us. Men began bringing extra dates, extra sawīq, and extra ghee, until they made a large heap of hays. They ate, then drank of rainwater beside them, and that was the wedding feast of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for her. We set out, and whenever we saw the walls of Madinah on a journey we would hasten toward them, urging our mounts, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urged his mount with Safiyyah behind him, as he had mounted her behind him. The mount of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stumbled, and he fell and she fell, with no one among the people looking at them until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and covered her. His Companions came to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was not harmed. We arrived at Madinah, and the young girls of his household came out to look at her, gloating over her fall."
"1284","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, who said: I said to Anas: O Abu Hamzah, narrate to us something of these wonders that you witnessed and do not narrate from anyone else. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the noon prayer one day, then went until he sat at the seats where Gabriel used to come to him. Bilal came and called for the afternoon prayer, and everyone who had family in Madinah stood to relieve himself and perform ablution, while some men of the Emigrants remained who had no families in Madinah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a wide cup containing water; he placed his palm in the vessel, but the vessel could not contain his whole palm, so he placed these four fingers in the vessel, then said: Draw near and perform ablution, with his hand in the vessel. They performed ablution until none of them remained without having performed ablution. I said: O Abu Hamzah, how many do you think they were? He said: Between seventy and eighty."
"1285","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: We were forbidden to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about anything, and it pleased us when an intelligent Bedouin man would come and ask him while we listened. A Bedouin man came and said: O Muhammad, your messenger came to us and claimed that you claim Allah sent you. He said: He spoke the truth. He said: Who created the heaven? He said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic. He said: Who created the earth? He said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic. He said: Who set up these mountains and placed in them what He placed? He said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic. He said: By the One who created the heaven and created the earth and set up these mountains and placed in them what He placed, has Allah sent you? He said: Yes. He said: Your messenger claimed that five prayers in our day and night are due upon us. He said: He spoke the truth. He said: By the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this? He said: Yes. Your messenger claimed that zakah on our wealth is due upon us. He said: He spoke the truth. He said: By the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this? He said: Yes. Your messenger claimed that fasting a month in our year is due upon us. He said: He spoke the truth. He said: By the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this? He said: Yes. Your messenger claimed that pilgrimage to the House is due upon us for whoever can find a way to it. He said: He spoke the truth. He said: Then he turned away and said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will neither add anything to them nor detract anything from them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he speaks the truth, he will enter Paradise."
"1286","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Trench, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was digging with us and carrying, until I could see the dust between his folds of skin and upon his skin, while we suffered hardship known to Allah the Exalted. Barley bread seasoned with rancid fat was brought to us, and we began eating with him eating alongside us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, true enjoyment is the enjoyment of the Hereafter."
"1287","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A boy was born to me tonight, and I named him after my father Ibrahim. Then he handed him to Umm Sayf, a wet-nurse in Madinah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to see him, and I went with him. We reached Abu Sayf while he was blowing his bellows with the house full of smoke. I hastened ahead of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Abu Sayf, hold back, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has come. So he held back, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, called for the boy, embraced him, and said what Allah willed him to say. Later I saw him struggling with his soul before him, and the eyes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shed tears. He said: The eye weeps, the heart grieves, and we say only what pleases our Lord. By Allah, O Ibrahim, we are grieved by you."
"1288","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Khaybar, al-Hajjaj ibn Ilat said: O Messenger of Allah, I have wealth in Makkah and family there, and I wish to go to them; am I free to speak against you or say something? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted him to say what he wished. He went to his wife when he arrived and said: Gather what you have, for I wish to buy from the spoils of Muhammad and his Companions, for they have been plundered and their wealth taken. This spread in Makkah, so the Muslims were downcast while the polytheists showed joy and delight. The news reached al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, and he was crippled in his sitting place, unable to stand. Mamar said: Uthman al-Jazari informed me, from Miqsam, who said: He took a son of his called Qutham, lay on his back, placed him on his chest, and said: Qutham the handsome. Mamar said: Thabit said, from Anas: Then he sent a slave boy of his to al-Hajjaj ibn Ilat, saying: Woe to you, what have you brought and what are you saying? What Allah has promised is better than what you have brought. Al-Hajjaj said to his slave boy: Convey greetings to Abu al-Fadl and tell him to leave one of his houses empty for me to visit him, for the news is what will please him. His slave boy came, and when he reached the door he said: Rejoice, O Abu al-Fadl. Al-Abbas leapt in joy and kissed him between the eyes, and he told him what al-Hajjaj had said, so he freed him. Then al-Hajjaj came and told him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had conquered Khaybar, taken its wealth as spoils, that the shares of Allah had been distributed from it, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had chosen Safiyyah bint Huyayy for himself and given her choice between being freed and becoming his wife or rejoining her family, and she chose to be freed and become his wife. But I have come for wealth I had here which I wished to collect and take away, so I asked permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he permitted me to say what I wished; so conceal this from me for three days, then mention what you will. His wife gathered what she had of jewelry and goods, collected it, and handed it to him, and he departed with it. After three days, al-Abbas went to the wife of al-Hajjaj and said: What did your husband do? She told him he had left on such-and-such day, and said: May Allah not grieve you, O Abu al-Fadl, we were distressed by what reached you. He said: Yes, may Allah not grieve me; by praise of Allah it was only what we loved. Al-Hajjaj has told me that Allah the Blessed and Exalted granted Khaybar to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the shares of Allah were distributed in it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) chose Safiyyah for himself. If you need your husband, join him. She said: By Allah, I think you are truthful. He said: I am truthful, and the matter is as I told you. Then he went to the gatherings of Quraysh while they said: Nothing but good befalls you, O Abu al-Fadl. He said: Nothing but good befell me, by praise of Allah. Al-Hajjaj ibn Ilat has told me that Allah the Mighty and Majestic granted Khaybar to His Messenger, the shares of the Muslims were distributed in it, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) chose Safiyyah for himself, and he asked me to conceal it from him for three days; he only came to take his wealth and what he had here, then leave. So Allah turned the gloom that had been upon the Muslims onto the polytheists. The Muslims who had entered their houses dejected came out until they reached al-Abbas, who told them the news, so the Muslims rejoiced, and whatever gloom, anger, or grief there was returned upon the polytheists."
"1289","Abu al-Walid informed me, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, who said: On the day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madinah, everything in it was illuminated; and on the day he passed away, everything was darkened. We were still burying him; we had not lifted our hands from his burial before we found our hearts changed."
"1290","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas: that a Persian man was a neighbor of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his broth had the finest aroma. He prepared food, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and invited him, with Aishah beside him, gesturing to him: Come. He said: And this one with me, pointing to Aishah. He said: No. Then he gestured a second time, and he said: And this one with me. He said: No. Then he gestured a third time, and he said: Yes. So Aishah went."
"1291","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, Maymun ibn Siyah, and Jafar ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those who frequent the houses of Allah are the people of Allah."
"1292","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, who said: I asked Anas: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) have a ring? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the night prayer one night until near half the night, then said: The people have prayed and slept, but you remain in prayer as long as you wait for it. Anas said: It is as though I still see the gleam of his silver ring, and he raised his left hand."
"1293","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed for rain and supplicated in this manner, spreading his hands and turning their backs toward his face."
"1294","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Aban, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): the same, except that he supplicated at Arafah."
"1295","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Urwah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): the same, that he prayed for rain with it."
"1296","Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik: that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, when will the Hour come, while beside him was an Ansari boy called Muhammad. He said: If this boy lives, he may not reach old age before the Hour comes."
"1297","Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik: that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the coming of the Hour. The prayer was then established, and when he finished his prayer he said: Where is the one who asked about the Hour? He said: Here I am, O Messenger of Allah. He said: What have you prepared for it? He said: I have not prepared much deed for it, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: A person is with the one he loves. Anas used to say: So we love Allah and His Messenger."
"1298","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah: I heard Thabit narrating from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come out to the mosque in which were the Emigrants and the Helpers, with none of them raising his head from his hunched sitting posture except Abu Bakr and Umar; he would smile at them and they would smile at him."
"1299","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would raid at dawn and listen; if he heard the call to prayer he held back, otherwise he raided."
"1300","Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: Thabit informed us, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would raid at the dawn prayer and would listen; if he heard the call to prayer, otherwise he raided. One day he listened and heard a man saying: Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great. He said: Upon the natural disposition. He said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. He said: You have come out of the Fire."
"1301","Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would often say: O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and shield us from the punishment of the Fire."
"1302","Sulayman ibn Harb and Abu al-Walid narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Every treacherous person has a banner on the Day of Resurrection by which he is known."
"1303","Said ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Thabit: I heard Anas saying: He would often say: O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and shield us from the punishment of the Fire. Shubah said: I said to Thabit: Is it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1304","Said ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would raise his hands in supplication until the whiteness of his armpits was seen. Shubah said: I mentioned that to Ali ibn Zayd, and he said: That is only in praying for rain. I said to him: Did you hear it from Anas? He said: Glory be to Allah. I said: Did you hear it from Anas? He said: Glory be to Allah, saying it two or three times."
"1305","Said ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: describing to us the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): when he raised his head from bowing he would stand until we said: He has forgotten."
"1306","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I love this chapter: Say, He is Allah, the One. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your love for it has admitted you to Paradise."
"1307","Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd and Thabit, from Anas, who said: I gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to drink in this cup every drink: honey, milk, nabidh, and water."
"1308","Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: Thabit al-Bunani informed me, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was playing with the boys when someone came, seized him, threw him down, opened his chest, took out the heart, then opened the heart and took out a clot from it, saying: This is the share of Satan from you. Then he washed it in a basin of gold with Zamzam water, closed it, and returned it to its place. The boys came running to his mother — meaning his nursing mother — saying: Muhammad has been killed. They came and met him pale in color. Anas said: We used to see the mark of that stitching on his chest."
"1309","Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that a man said: O our master and son of our master, and O our best and son of our best. He said: O people, keep to your speech, and let not Satan mislead you. I am Muhammad ibn Abdullah."
"1310","Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There will remain of Paradise what Allah wills to remain, then Allah the Exalted will create for it whatever creation He wills."
"1311","Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit and Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and the Fire is surrounded by desires."
"1312","Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani and Abu Imran, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Imran said: Four will come out of the Fire, while Thabit said: Two men. They will be presented before Allah the Mighty and Majestic, then they will be ordered into the Fire. One of them will turn and say: My Lord, when You took me out of it, I had hoped You would not return me to it. So Allah will save him from it."
"1313","Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The most afflicted person in the world among the people of Paradise will be brought, and Allah will say to him: Dip him once in Paradise. He will be dipped in it, then come out, and He will say: O son of Adam, did you ever see misery or anything you disliked? He will say: No. Then the most favored person in the world among the people of the Fire will be brought, and Allah the Mighty and Majestic will say: O son of Adam, did you ever see any good or any delight? He will say: No, by Your might."
"1314","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw tonight in a sleeper's dream as though we were in the house of Uqbah ibn Rafi, and we were brought fresh dates of Ibn Tab. I interpreted it as eminence for us in this world, a good outcome in the Hereafter, and that our religion has become good."
"1315","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The she-camel of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), al-Adba, was never beaten. A Bedouin came and raced her on a young camel of his, and the Bedouin beat her. It weighed heavily upon the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is a right upon Allah that no worldly thing rises but He lowers it."
"1316","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked pumpkin. When it was served, the pumpkin would be pushed toward the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1317","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was frightened though no one is frightened, and I was harmed for Allah though no one is harmed. Thirty days and nights passed over me while neither Bilal nor I had food fit for a living being except something concealed in the armpit of Bilal."
"1318","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: that some men among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about his private worship. One of them said: I will not sleep on a bed; another said: I will not marry women; another said: I will fast and never break my fast. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he stood to deliver a sermon, praised Allah the Mighty and Majestic and extolled Him, then said: To proceed, what is with people who said such-and-such? But I fast and break my fast, sleep and pray, and marry women. Whoever turns away from my practice is not from me."
"1319","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say while digging the Trench, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say. Barley bread with rancid melted fat was brought, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: True good is the good of the Hereafter."
"1320","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: that the wives of the Prophet would go out early on the day of Uhud carrying water skins on their backs, with their shins visible, giving drink."
"1321","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: I took Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was born, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in a cloak smearing a camel of his. He said: Do you have dates with you? I said: Yes. I handed him some dates; he chewed them, opened his mouth, spat them into his, and he began to smack his lips. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The beloved of the Ansar is dates. And he named him Abdullah."
"1322","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast until it was said: He fasts, he fasts; and he would break his fast until it was said: He breaks his fast, he breaks his fast."
"1323","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he gave him sheep. He went to his people and said: O people, embrace Islam, for by Allah, Muhammad gives the giving of one who does not fear poverty. A man would come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanting nothing thereby but the world, yet by evening his religion would be dearer to him than the world and what is in it."
"1324","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The prayer was established one night, and a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a need. So he stood conversing with him until the people, or some of the people, dozed. Then he prayed with them, and no ablution was mentioned."
"1325","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl and Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited all his wives in a single day."
"1326","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl and Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed on a mat, with Umm Sulaym and Umm Haram behind us, and he placed them on his right, as Thabit thought."
"1327","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a sword on the day of Uhud and said: Who will take this sword with its right? One said: I, another said: I, another said: I. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Which of you will take it with its right? They held back. Simak Abu Dujanah said: I will take it, O Messenger of Allah. He took it and split the heads of the polytheists on the day of Uhud."
"1328","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three qualities, whoever has them finds the sweetness of faith: that Allah and His Messenger are dearer to him than all else; that he loves a servant only for Allah the Mighty and Majestic; and that being thrown into the Fire is dearer to him than returning to Judaism or Christianity."
"1329","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man of the people of Paradise will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and Allah the Exalted will say: O son of Adam, how did you find your dwelling? He will say: My Lord, the best dwelling. It will be said: Wish and ask. He will say: I wish and ask for nothing except to be returned to the world and killed ten times — for what he sees of the virtue of martyrdom. Then a man of the people of the Fire will be brought, and He will say to him: O son of Adam, how did you find your dwelling? He will say: My Lord, the worst dwelling. It will be said: Would you ransom yourself from it with gold filling the earths? He will say: Yes. Allah the Mighty and Majestic will say: You lie; I asked you for what was easier than that, but you did not do it."
"1330","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that a youth of Aslam said: O Messenger of Allah, I wish to fight but I have nothing to equip myself with. He said: A certain Ansari had been equipping himself but fell ill; go to him and say to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conveys greetings to you and says to you: Hand over to me what you equipped yourself with. He went to him and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conveys greetings to you and says to you: Hand over to me what you equipped yourself with. He said: O so-and-so, hand over to him what you equipped me with, and withhold nothing of it; by Allah, withhold nothing of it, that we may be blessed therein."
"1331","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Umarah ibn Zadham al-Saydalani narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: I had a brother, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would greet him and say: O Abu Umayr, what happened to the little sparrow?"
"1332","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Talhah ibn Amr narrated to us, saying: Thabit al-Bunani informed me, saying: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come out to us after sunset and before the sunset prayer and see us praying, neither forbidding us nor commanding us."
"1333","Abu Ishaq Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami informed us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit and Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik: that when Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf arrived in Madinah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between him and Sad ibn al-Rabi. Sad said to him: O my brother, I am among the wealthiest people of Madinah; look at half my wealth and take it, and I have two wives — look at whichever of them you wish so I may release her for you. He said: May Allah bless your family and wealth for you; show me the market. They showed him the market, so he bought and sold and profited, and came back with some ghee and dried curds. Then he stayed as long as Allah willed, then came with traces of saffron on him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Mahyam? He said: I have married a woman. He said: What did you give her as dowry? He said: The weight of a date pit in gold. He said: Give a wedding feast, even with a sheep. Abd al-Rahman said: After that I saw myself — if I lifted a stone, I would think I would find gold or silver beneath it."
"1334","al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas: that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has a palm tree, and I can only complete my wall with it; order him to give it to me so I may complete my wall with it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Give it to him for a palm tree in Paradise, but he refused. Abu al-Dahdah came to him and said: Sell me your palm tree for my walled garden. He did so. Then he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have bought the palm tree with my walled garden; assign it to him, and I have given it to you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How many heavy clusters laden with dates for Abu al-Dahdah in Paradise — saying it repeatedly. Then he went to his wife and said: O Umm al-Dahdah, leave the walled garden, for I have sold it for a palm tree in Paradise. She said: A profitable sale, or a word like it."
"1335","al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to his bed, he would say: Praise be to Allah who fed us, gave us drink, sufficed us, and sheltered us; how many have neither suffice nor shelter."
"1336","al-Hasan ibn Musa informed us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ammar ibn Abi Ammar informed us, from Abbas — and Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver the sermon leaning on a palm trunk. When the pulpit was made, he moved to the pulpit, and the trunk moaned until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to it and embraced it, and it fell quiet. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I not embraced it, it would have moaned until the Day of Resurrection. [Print note: thus in the Alam al-Kutub edition; the correct reading is Ibn Abbas, as in Musnad Ahmad and others — omitted from translation as print apparatus.]"
"1337","al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that a man said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O our best and son of our best, and O our master and son of our master. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep to your speech, and let not Satan mislead you. I am Muhammad ibn Abdullah, the servant of Allah and His Messenger. By Allah, I do not like you to raise me above the station Allah has given me."
"1338","al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed for rain and pointed with the backs of his hands toward the sky."
"1339","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Thabit, from Anas: that a man stood before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? The people pulled him and seated him. Then he stood a second time and asked him, and the people pulled him and seated him. Then he stood a third time and said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: Woe to you, what have you prepared for it? He said: Love of Allah and His Messenger. The Prophet said to him: Sit, for you are with the one you love. Anas ibn Malik said: We never rejoiced after Islam as we rejoiced at his saying: Sit, for you are with the one you love. He said: I hope to be with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar for my love of them, though I fall short of their deeds."
"1340","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not go beyond his ears."
"1341","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the most handsome of people, the most generous of people, and the bravest of people. The people of Madinah were frightened one night, so we went out toward the sound, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met them on a bare horse of Abu Talhah with the sword around his neck, having already investigated the news, saying: Do not be alarmed, do not be alarmed. Then he said: We found it swift. Hammad said: It was a horse that used to be slow, yet it was never outrun after that day. Hammad said: This is in the hadith of Thabit or in the hadith of another."
"1342","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, and from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey, and a black boy called Anjashah was chanting for them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gently, woe to you, O Anjashah, your driving of the glass vessels. Abu Qilabah said: Meaning the women."
"1343","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: al-Bara would chant for the men, and Anjashah would chant for the women, and he had a beautiful voice. He chanted, and the camels quickened their pace. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gently, O Anjashah, woe to you, your driving of the glass vessels. Abu Qilabah said: Meaning the women."
"1344","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), al-Adba, was never beaten. A Bedouin came on a young camel of his, raced her, and beat her. It weighed heavily upon the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is a right upon Allah that no worldly thing rises but He lowers it."
"1345","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the people of Yemen came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, send with us a man to teach us the Quran. He took the hand of Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah and sent him with them, saying: This is the trustee of this nation."
"1346","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and heard a movement. I said: What is this? They said: This is Bilal. Then I entered Paradise and heard a movement. I said: What is this? They said: This is Bilal. Then I entered Paradise and heard a movement. I said: What is this? They said: This is al-Ghumaysa bint Milhan, Umm Sulaym, the mother of Anas ibn Malik."
"1347","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that Abu Talhah would shoot before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud, and he was a skilled archer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was behind him, and when he shot, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would raise his figure to see where his arrow landed. Abu Talhah would push back the chest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his hand, saying: O Messenger of Allah, thus — no arrow will strike you. Abu Talhah shielded himself before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, I am strong and sturdy, so direct me to your needs and send me where you wish."
"1348","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Uhud: O Allah, if You will, You will not be worshipped on earth."
"1349","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that a woman of unsound mind said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a need. He stood and said: O mother of so-and-so, choose whichever road you wish so I may attend to your need with you. He did not leave her until her need was fulfilled."
"1350","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the sister of al-Rubayyi, Umm Harithah, wounded a person, and the case was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Retaliation. Umm Harithah said: Will retaliation be taken from so-and-so? By Allah, retaliation will not be taken from her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Umm Harithah, it is the decree of Allah the Exalted. She said: No, by Allah, retaliation will not be taken from her. Then they spoke to the people until they made peace with them and they accepted blood money. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the servants of Allah are those who, if they swear upon Allah, Allah fulfills it."
"1351","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik: that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to his bed, he would say: Praise be to Allah who fed us, gave us drink, sufficed us, and sheltered us; how many have neither suffice nor shelter."
"1352","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate food, he would lick his three fingers, and he said: When a morsel falls from one of you, let him take it, remove the harm from it, eat it, and not leave it for Satan. He would command us to wipe the dish clean, saying: None of you knows in which part of his food the blessing lies."
"1353","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted continuously, and some of his Companions fasted continuously. He said: If the month were extended for me, I would fast continuously in a manner that would make the extremists abandon their extremism. I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink."
"1354","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that a man used to write the Quran for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he dictated to him All-Hearing, All-Knowing, he would write All-Hearing, All-Seeing, or the like. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: What did you write? He would say: Such-and-such. He would say: Leave it. He had recited al-Baqarah and Al Imran, and whoever recited them had recited much of the Quran. Later he left and said: I am the most knowledgeable of people about Muhammad; he would dictate to me and I would write other than what he said. He would say to me: What did you write? I would say: Such-and-such, and he would say: Leave it. Then he died, and the earth cast him out; then he was buried, and the earth cast him out. Abu Talhah said: I went until I saw him cast out."
"1355","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he gave him sheep. He returned to his people and said: O people, come to Muhammad, for by Allah, he gives the giving of one who does not fear poverty. Anas said: A man would come wanting nothing but the world, yet by evening his religion would be dearer to him than the world and what is in it."
"1356","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, who said: Anas said: Umm Sulaym had a cup, and there was no drink but I gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to drink from it: water, honey, milk, and nabidh."
"1357","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik: that a funeral passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they praised him with good, so he said: It is due. They passed with another funeral and praised it with evil, so he said: It is due. Then he said: You are the witnesses of Allah on earth."
"1358","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Such was the ring of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and he gestured with his left hand, placing his thumb on the back of his little finger."
"1359","Amr ibn Asim narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit and Humayd, from Anas, who said: The inscription on the ring of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah."
"1360","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) strove in supplication for someone, he would say: May Allah place upon you the prayer of a righteous people who stand the night and fast the day, who are neither sinful nor wicked."
"1361","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: I served the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for ten years, and he never once said to me Uff, nor said about something I did: Why did you do so, nor about something I did not do: Why did you not do so."
"1362","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit: Anas was asked about the dyeing of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: He did not see enough white hair to dye; had I wished, I could count the white hairs in his beard. The dye of Abu Bakr was with henna and katam, and the dye of Umar was with henna."
"1363","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: I never touched silk or brocade, nor anything softer than the palm of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor ever smelled a scent — or he said: a fragrance — more pleasant than the scent — or he said: the fragrance — of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1364","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grew heavy with illness, Fatimah said: O the distress of my father. He said to her: Your father will have no distress after today. When he died, Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: O my father, he answered a Lord who called him; O my father, the Garden of Firdaws is his abode; O my father, to Gabriel we announce his death; O my father, how near he is to his Lord. When he was buried, Fatimah said: O Anas, could your hearts bear throwing dust upon the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"
"1365","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for water, and water was brought in a wide cup. He placed his palm in it — it is as though I still see the water springing from between his fingers like springs. He said: I estimated the people between seventy and eighty."
"1366","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When is the Hour? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What have you prepared for it? He said: Nothing, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A person is with the one he loves. Anas said: We never rejoiced at anything as we rejoiced at the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A person is with the one he loves. Anas said: I love the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I love Abu Bakr and Umar, and I hope to be with them for my love of them, though I do not do deeds like theirs."
"1367","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw traces of yellow dye on Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and said to him: What is this? He said: I have married a woman for the weight of a date pit in gold. He said: May Allah bless you; give a wedding feast, even with a sheep."
"1368","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) give a wedding feast for any of his wives like the one he gave for Zaynab; he feasted with a sheep."
"1369","1369 - Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, he said: Yusuf ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, he said: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that a woman was married to a man and her father fell ill, so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is ill and my husband refuses to permit me to nurse him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Obey your husband. Then her father died, and she asked her husband's permission to pray over him, but her husband refused to permit her to pray. So she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Obey your husband. So she obeyed her husband and did not pray over her father. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Allah has forgiven your father on account of your obedience to your husband."
"1370","1370 - Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, he said: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon a man while he was dying, and said to him: How do you find yourself? He said: I hope and I fear. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These two do not gather in the heart of a servant at such a moment except that Allah grants him what he hopes for and secures him from what he fears."
"1371","1371 - Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, he said: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would hear the crying of a child with his mother while he was in prayer, or something in the prayer, and he would recite a short surah."
"1372","1372 - Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer should not wish for death because of some harm that has befallen him; but if he must do so, or if you must do so, let him say: O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is good for me, and take me in death when death is good for me."
"1373","1373 - Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he would frequently say: Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and shield us from the punishment of the Fire. He said: So I said to Thabit: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1374","1374 - Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi informed me, he said: al-Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, here is a man who does not pray any prayer except that he recites in it: Say, He is Allah, the One, sometimes reciting it alone and sometimes reciting it with another surah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What do you intend by this? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I love it. He said: Then your love of it has admitted you into Paradise."
"1375","1375 - Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Thabit and Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on an errand, and I saw children playing, so I sat with them. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and greeted the children."
"1376","1376 - Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O so-and-so, did you do such-and-such? He said: No, by the One besides whom there is no god, I did not do it, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew that he had done it. He repeated that to him three times, each time he swore while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew that he had done it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Allah has expiated your lie by your truthfulness in saying: There is no god but Allah."
"1377","1377 - Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas, who said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, when we are with you we are in one state, but when we leave you we are in a different state, and we fear that this is hypocrisy. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: How are you with regard to your Lord? They said: Allah is our Lord in secret and in public. He said: How are you with regard to your Prophet? They said: You are our Prophet in secret and in public. He said: That is not hypocrisy."
"1378","1378 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, and I think only from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever raises two daughters or two sisters or three until they separate (by marriage) or he dies leaving them, I and he will be in Paradise like these two - and he joined his two fingers together."
"1379","1379 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit and Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb and Shuayb ibn al-Habhab, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and made her freedom her dowry. He said: Then I heard Abd al-Aziz ask Thabit, saying: O Abu Muhammad, did you ask Anas about this hadith, what did he give her as dowry? He said: Herself."
"1380","1380 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: I do not refrain from praying with you as I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray. He said: And when Anas bowed and then stood upright, he would not prostrate until someone would say - or we would say: He has forgotten. And when he prostrated and raised his head, he would not prostrate (the second time) until someone would say - or we would say: He has forgotten."
"1381","1381 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that a Bedouin came to the mosque of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and urinated in it, so a man rushed toward him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him, do not interrupt him. He said: Then he called for a bucket of water or a pail of water and poured it over it."
"1382","1382 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, who said: A funeral passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and it was praised with good, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has become due. Then another funeral passed and it was spoken of with evil, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has become due. It was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, you said of this one: It has become due, and you said of this one: It has become due. He said: Indeed the people, or the believers, are the witnesses of Allah on earth."
"1383","1383 - Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to me, he said: Umarah ibn Zadham narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that when Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf emigrated, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between him and Sad ibn al-Rabi. He said to him: I have two gardens, so choose whichever of my two gardens you wish. He said: May Allah bless your two gardens for you; that is not why I accepted Islam. Show me the market. He said: So he showed him, and he used to buy clarified butter and dried yogurt and hides, and he accumulated wealth and married. Then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a trace of yellow perfume on him, and he said: What is this? He said: I have married. He said: May Allah bless you; give a wedding feast even with a sheep. He said: Then his wealth grew until seven hundred camels carrying cloth and flour and food came to him. He said: When they entered Madinah, a loud noise was heard among the people of Madinah. Aishah said: What is this noise? It was said to her: A caravan belonging to Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf has arrived, seven hundred camels carrying cloth and flour and food. Aishah said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: And Abd al-Rahman will not enter Paradise except crawling. When that reached Abd al-Rahman, he said: O mother, I make you witness that they with their loads and saddles and packs are in the cause of Allah Almighty."
"1384","1384 - Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The voice of Abu Talhah is more severe upon the polytheists than a troop."
"1385","1385 - Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, he said: Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, from Humayd, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two white-black horned rams."
"1386","1386 - Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah Almighty fashioned Adam in Paradise, He left him as long as He willed to leave him. Iblis began to circle around him looking at what he was. When he saw him hollow, he knew that he was created as a creation that does not control itself."
"1387","1387 - Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, he said: al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit and Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas: that when the polytheists overwhelmed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud, he said: Who will repel them from us, and he will be my companion in Paradise? A man from the Ansar stood and fought until he was killed. Then another stood repelling them and fought until seven were killed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: We have not done justice to our companions."
"1388","1388 - Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, he said: Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Umarah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Umm Sulaym to look at a woman. He said: Smell her mouth and look at her ankles."
"1389","1389 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that Abdullah ibn Salam came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he arrived in Madinah, and said: I am going to ask you about three things which none knows except a prophet. He said: Ask. He said: What is the first of the matters of the Hour, or the signs of the Hour, and what is the first food the people of Paradise will eat, and what causes the child to resemble his father and the child to resemble his mother? He said: Jibril informed me of them just now. He said: Jibril? He said: Yes. He said: He is the enemy of the Jews among the angels. He said: As for the first of the signs of the Hour, it is a fire that will come out from the east and gather the people toward the west. As for the first food the people of Paradise will eat, it is the extra lobe of the fish's liver. As for what causes the child to resemble his father and the child to resemble his mother, when the man's fluid precedes the woman's fluid it resembles his father, and when the woman's fluid precedes the man's fluid it resembles his mother. He said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews are a people of slander, so hide me from them, then ask them about me before they learn of my Islam: what kind of man am I among them? Then a group of them came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: What kind of man is Abdullah among you? They said: The best of us and the son of the best of us, our master and the son of our master, the most learned of us and the son of the most learned of us. He said: What would you think if Abdullah accepted Islam? They said: May Allah protect him from that. He said: Then Abdullah came out to them and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. They said: The worst of us and the son of the worst of us, and the like of that. Abdullah says: O Messenger of Allah, this is what I feared."
"1390","1390 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf emigrated to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he established brotherhood between him and Sad ibn al-Rabi. Sad said to him: O Abd al-Rahman, I am among the wealthiest of the Ansar, and I will share my wealth with you, and I have two wives and I will divorce one of them, so when her waiting period ends, marry her. Abd al-Rahman said to him: May Allah bless your family and your wealth for you, but show me the market. So he showed him, and he did not return that day until he had gained something of clarified butter and dried yogurt as profit. He remained for some days, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him and saw a trace of yellow perfume on him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What is this? He said: I have married, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Whom? He said: A woman from the Ansar. He said: What did you give her as dowry? He said: A date-stone's weight, or the weight of a date-stone, of gold. He said: Give a wedding feast even with a sheep."
"1391","1391 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: that Abu Musa asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a mount, and he met with some preoccupation from him, so he swore that he would not provide him a mount, then he provided him a mount. He said: O Messenger of Allah, you swore that you would not provide me a mount. He said: And I swear that I will provide you a mount; and he provided him a mount."
"1392","1392 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd informed us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madinah while they had two days in which they would play. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have come to you while you had two days in which you play, and Allah the Blessed and Exalted has replaced them for you with two days better than them: the day of Fitr and the day of Adha."
"1393","1393 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd informed us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You need not admire anyone until you see with what he is sealed. For a worker works for a period of his life, or a span of his time, with righteous deeds, such that if he died upon them he would enter Paradise, then he changes and works evil deeds. And a servant works for a period of his life with evil deeds, such that if he died upon them he would enter the Fire, then he changes and works righteous deeds. And when Allah intends good for a servant, He employs him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how does He employ him? He said: He wakes him for a righteous deed, then takes him (in death) upon it."
"1394","1394 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Whenever we wished to see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night praying, we saw him, and whenever we wished to see him at night sleeping, we saw him sleeping."
"1395","1395 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, Anas narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast in the month until we would say: He does not break fast in any part of it; and he would break fast until we would say: He does not fast in any part of it."
"1396","1396 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas: that his uncle was absent from the fighting at Badr, and said: I was absent from the first battle the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fought against the polytheists; if Allah Almighty makes me witness a battle, Allah will see how I act. When the day of Uhud came and the Muslims were exposed, he said: O Allah, I disavow to You what these have brought - meaning the polytheists - and I apologize to You for what these have done - meaning his companions. Then he advanced, and Sad met him at the far side short of Uhud. I said: I am with you. He said: I could not do what he did. He was found with more than eighty sword strikes and spear thrusts and arrow shots. He said: And we used to say concerning him and his companions was revealed: Among them are those who fulfilled their vow and among them are those who wait. He said: meaning the verse."
"1397","1397 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd informed us, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would supplicate with this supplication: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from worry and grief and laziness and old age and incapacity."
"1398","1398 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd informed us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should wish for death because of a harm that has befallen him or will befall him; rather let him say: O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is good for me, and take me in death when You know death is good for me."
"1399","1399 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd informed us, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a man who had become like a plucked chick, and said: Did you supplicate with anything or ask Him for anything? He said: I said: O Allah, whatever punishment You will inflict upon me in the Hereafter, hasten it for me in this world. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glory be to Allah, then you cannot bear that, and you will never be able to. Why did you not say: Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and shield us from the punishment of the Fire."
"1400","1400 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd and Yahya al-Sawwaf together informed us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the best quarters of the Ansar? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The quarters of Banu al-Najjar, then the quarters of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then the quarters of Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, then the quarters of Banu Saidah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And in all the quarters of the Ansar there is good. One of the two said: And he raised his voice with it."
"1401","1401 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from al-Hasan and Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Help your brother whether he is an oppressor or oppressed. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we help him when he is oppressed, but how do we help him when he is an oppressor? He said: You prevent him from oppression."
"1402","1402 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd informed us, from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from the expedition of Tabuk and drew near Madinah, he said: Indeed in Madinah there are people: you did not travel any journey nor cross any valley except that they were with you in it. They said: O Messenger of Allah, while they are in Madinah? He said: Yes, excuse detained them."
"1403","1403 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd informed us, from Anas, who said: Abu Taybah cupped the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered two measures of food for him, and spoke to his masters on his behalf, so they reduced his tax. And he said: The best of what you treat yourselves with is cupping and Indian costus, and do not torture your children by pressing for throat ailment."
"1404","1404 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd informed us, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque and saw a rope stretched between two pillars. He said: What is this rope? They said: It belongs to so-and-so; she prays, and when she is overcome she clings to it. He said: Let her pray as long as she understands; when she fears being overcome, let her sleep."
"1405","1405 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd informed us, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while at Badr, the Muslims heard him calling: O Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, and O Utbah ibn Rabiah, and O Shaybah ibn Rabiah, and O Umayyah ibn Khalaf, have you found what your Lord promised you to be true? For I have found what my Lord promised me to be true. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you are calling a people who have decayed. He said: You are not more hearing of what I say than them, but they are unable to answer."
"1406","1406 - Yazid informed us, he said: Humayd informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: that after the prayer had been established and before he said the takbir, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to the people with his face and said: Straighten your rows and stand close together, for I see you from behind my back. Indeed one of us would join his shoulder to his brother's shoulder and his foot to his foot and his knee to his knee in prayer."
"1407","1407 - Yazid informed us, he said: Humayd informed us, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved that the Emigrants and the Helpers be next to him so that they would learn from him."
"1408","1408 - Yazid informed us, he said: Humayd informed us, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at al-Baqi when a man called out to a man: O Abu al-Qasim. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not mean you; I only meant so-and-so. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunyah."
"1409","1409 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd informed us, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying one night in his chamber, and some of his companions came to him and prayed with his prayer, so he shortened it. Then he entered the house, then came out, and did that repeatedly, each time praying and entering. When morning came, they said: O Messenger of Allah, we prayed with you and we would like you to lengthen your prayer. He said: I knew of your place, and I did that deliberately."
"1410","1410 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come a people whose hearts are more tender than yours. Then the Asharis came, among them Abu Musa, and they began to chant rajaz and say: [poetry omitted in the source text]."
"1411","1411 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man while he was driving a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial animal. He said: Ride it."
"1412","1412 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until none says on earth: Allah, Allah."
"1413","1413 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas: he said: When this verse was revealed: You will never attain righteousness until you spend of what you love, or: Who is it that will lend Allah a good loan, Abu Talhah said: O Messenger of Allah, my garden in such-and-such a place belongs to Allah Almighty, and if I could keep it secret I would not announce it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Place it among your relatives or kinsfolk."
"1414","1414 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, he said: Anas was asked: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dye his hair? He said: Gray hair did not disfigure him. It was said: Is graying a disfigurement? He said: All of you dislike it; there were only some hairs at the front of his beard, and he pointed to the front of his beard."
"1415","1415 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd informed us, from Anas: that a son of Umm Sulaym was called Abu Umayr, and he had a small bird called nughayr. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her, he would joke with him. He entered upon her and saw him sad, and said: What is wrong with Abu Umayr? She said: O Messenger of Allah, his nughayr has died. He said: So he began to say: O Abu Umayr, what happened to the nughayr?"
"1416","1416 - Abu Wahb Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi informed us, he said: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Abu Talhah had a son called Abu Umayr, and he had a nughayr with which he would play. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would speak affectionately to him when he entered. He came and his nughayr had died, and he saw him sad, and said: What is wrong with Abu Umayr? They said: O Messenger of Allah, his nughayr has died. He said: O Abu Umayr, what happened to the nughayr?"
"1417","1417 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd informed us, he said: Anas was asked: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raise his hands when he supplicated? He said: Yes, that was on the day of Friday when rain was withheld and the land became barren and wealth perished. He raised his hands until I saw the whiteness of his armpits, while I did not see a cloud in the sky. He prayed for rain, and he had not finished the prayer before even a youth living nearby would be concerned about returning to his family. It continued for a week. When the next Friday came, they said: O Messenger of Allah, houses have collapsed and riders have been held back and wealth has perished. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled, then said with his hands: O Allah, around us and not upon us. He said: So it cleared away from Madinah."
"1418","1418 - Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Muhammad ibn Thabit, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man says to his brother: May Allah reward you with good, he has excelled in praise."
"1419","1419 - Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Muhammad ibn Thabit, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, benefit me by what You have taught me, and teach me what benefits me, and increase me in knowledge. Praise be to Allah in every circumstance. My Lord, I seek refuge in You from the state of the people of the Fire."
"1420","1420 - Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah, Sad Abu Mujahid al-Tai narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mudallah, the freedman of the Mother of the Believers, narrated to me that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: We said: O Messenger of Allah, when we are with you our hearts become tender and we are of the people of the Hereafter, but when we leave you and smell women and children, this world pleases us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, if you remained as you are with me, the angels would shake hands with you with their palms and visit you in your houses. And if you did not sin, Allah would bring a people who sin and seek forgiveness, and He would forgive them. We said: O Messenger of Allah, tell us about Paradise: of what is its building? He said: A brick of gold and a brick of silver, its pebbles are pearls and rubies, its mortar is musk, and its soil is saffron. Whoever enters it will live in bliss and never suffer, and will abide forever and never die. His clothes will never wear out, and his youth will never perish. Three whose supplication is not rejected: the fasting person until he breaks his fast, the just ruler, and the supplication of the oppressed. It is carried upon the clouds, the gates of heaven are opened for it, and the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, says: By My Might, I will surely help you even after a while."
"1421","1421 - Abu Asim informed us, from al-Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, from Ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Jafar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three supplications are answered, there is no doubt in them: the supplication of the father against his child, the supplication of the oppressed, and the supplication of the traveler."
"1422","1422 - Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Nahhas ibn Qahm narrated to us, from Shaddad Abu Ammar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever guards the voluntary forenoon prayer, his sins will be forgiven even if they are more than the foam of the sea."
"1423","1423 - Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The best fasting after Ramadan is the month of Allah, al-Muharram, and the best prayer after the obligatory is the night prayer."
"1424","1424 - Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Musa, Muhammad ibn Wasi narrated to us, from Shutayr ibn Nahar al-Abdi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord Almighty said: If My servants obeyed Me, I would give them rain at night, and bring out the sun upon them by day, and I would not let them hear the sound of thunder. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Renew your faith. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how do we renew our faith? He said: Say frequently: There is no god but Allah."
"1425","1425 - Affan ibn Muslim and Abu al-Walid informed us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Wasi, from Shutayr ibn Nahar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good opinion is part of good worship."
"1426","1426 - Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from a man, from Abu Hurayrah: that a man complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the hardness of his heart. He said: If you want your heart to soften, feed the poor and wipe the head of the orphan."
"1427","1427 - Abd al-Malik ibn Amr al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from Musa ibn Abi Uthman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah Almighty created Adam in His image."
"1428","1428 - Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ulayy narrated to us, from his father, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Marwan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The worst thing in a man is intense miserliness and cowardice that unnerves."
"1429","1429 - Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions giving them glad tidings: Ramadan has come to you, a blessed month; Allah has obligated its fasting upon you. In it the gates of Paradise are opened, and in it the gates of Hell are closed, and in it the devils are chained. In it is a night better than a thousand months; whoever is deprived of its good has indeed been deprived."
"1430","1430 - Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Asid, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of envy, for envy devours good deeds just as fire devours wood - or he said: grass."
"1431","1431 - Abd al-Malik ibn Amr and Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man follows the religion of his close friend, so let one of you look at whom he befriends."
"1432","1432 - Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed in Paradise there are columns of ruby, upon them chambers of emerald; they have open doors shining like the brilliant star shines. We said: O Messenger of Allah, who will dwell in them? He said: Those who love one another for the sake of Allah Almighty, and sit together for the sake of Allah Almighty, and meet one another for the sake of Allah Almighty."
"1433","1433 - Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Hajjaj ibn Furafisah, from Makhul, from Abu Hurayrah, raising it (to the Prophet), he said: Whoever seeks the world lawfully, to refrain from begging, and striving for his family, and being kind to his neighbor, will come on the Day of Resurrection with his face like the moon on the night of full moon. And whoever seeks the world lawfully out of boasting and rivalry and showing off will meet Allah Almighty while He is angry with him."
"1434","1434 - Umar ibn Said al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Tanukhi narrated to us, from Makhul, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not fight, nor equip a fighter, nor take the place of a fighter in the path of Allah among his family with good, Allah will afflict him with a calamity."
"1435","1435 - Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from a man, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until a man passes by his brother's grave and says: Would that I were in his place."
"1436","1436 - Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Umayyah narrated to us, from Abu Amr ibn Muhammad ibn Hurayth, from his grandfather Hurayth, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you prays, let him place something in front of him; if he does not find, let him erect a stick; if he does not find, let him draw a line. Then whoever passes in front of him will not harm him."
"1437","1437 - Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Mansur, from Abbad ibn Unays, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The caller to prayer is forgiven as far as his voice reaches, and everything moist and dry that hears him confirms him. And for the one who witnesses (the prayer) with him there are twenty-five good deeds."
"1438","1438 - Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Aban, from al-Ala ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the most beloved of Allah's servants to Allah are those who observe the sun and the moon."
"1439","1439 - Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Abi Anas, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the month of Ramadan enters, the gates of Hell are closed, the gates of mercy are opened, and the devils are chained."
"1440","1440 - Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, that Muhammad ibn Amr informed him that Salamah ibn al-Azraq was sitting with Ibn Umar when a funeral passed by while women were weeping over it. Ibn Umar disapproved of that and rebuked them. Salamah ibn al-Azraq said to him: Do not say this, O Abu Abd al-Rahman, for I bear witness that I heard Abu Hurayrah say: A funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was with him, along with Umar ibn al-Khattab, and women weeping over it. Umar scolded them and rebuked them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave them, O Umar, for the eye sheds tears, the soul is afflicted, and the covenant is recent. Ibn Umar said: Allah and His Messenger know best, Allah and His Messenger know best."
"1441","1441 - Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Hisham ibn Yahya, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man becomes bankrupt and the seller finds his goods intact, he has more right to them than the other creditors."
"1442","1442 - Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, he said: Abu Said, the freedman of Abdullah ibn Amir, narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not engage in false bidding, do not hate one another, do not turn away from one another, do not envy one another, and let none of you sell over the sale of another. Be servants of Allah as brothers. The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim: he does not wrong him, nor forsake him, nor despise him. Piety is here - pointing to his chest. Everything of the Muslim is forbidden to the Muslim: his blood and his honor. It suffices a man that he despises his Muslim brother."
"1443","1443 - Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yaqub informed me, from Abu Abdullah, that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun does not rise nor set upon a day better than Friday. There is no creature except that it is frightened on Friday except these two burdens: the jinn and mankind. Upon every gate of the mosque there are two angels writing the first then the first: like a man who offered a camel, and like a man who offered a cow, and like a man who offered a sheep, and like a man who offered a bird, and like a man who offered an egg. When the imam sits, the scrolls are folded."
"1444","1444 - Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Furat al-Tamimi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Luqman narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari, from Abu Hurayrah: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Eating in the markets is baseness."
"1445","1445 - Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Imran al-Qattan, from Qatadah, from Abbas al-Jushami, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed a surah from the Book of Allah Almighty, which is thirty verses, interceded for a man and brought him out of the Fire and admitted him into Paradise, and it is the surah Tabarak."
"1446","1446 - Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Mihran narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Amir al-Uqayli, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first to enter Paradise are three: a servant who perfected the worship of his Lord and fulfilled the rights of his masters, a poor man who is chaste and refrains, and a man who fought in the cause of Allah until he was killed. And the first to enter the Fire are three: a poor man who is boastful, a ruler given power, and a wealthy man who did not fulfill the rights of his wealth."
"1447","1447 - Yaqub ibn Ibrahim al-Zuhri informed us, he said: my father narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - and Allah knows best: Forbidden for two eyes to be touched by the Fire: an eye that wept out of fear of Allah Almighty, and an eye that spent the night guarding Islam and its people against the people of disbelief. And he said: No servant weeps and his eyes shed tears out of fear of Allah and then He admits him into the Fire ever, until the rain returns to the sky. And it is said: He stood upon the pulpit when the people returned from Mutah with a piece of bread in his hand. When he mentioned their affair, his eyes overflowed, so he wiped his face and said: I am only a human being; I seek refuge in Allah from Satan. A man sees that he is many through his brother. Whoever has a promise with me - Salman al-Farisi said: I do, O Messenger of Allah - so he gave it to him. And Barakah said, when the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who was married to Uthman was dying while he was present: his eyes overflowed and Barakah wept and tore her hair, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rebuked her. She said: Do you weep, O Messenger of Allah, while we are silent? He said: What you saw from me is mercy for her; I am only a human being. Indeed the believer is in every good station with Allah, whether in hardship or ease."
"1448","1448 - Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to me, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile the rooster, for it wakes for prayer."
"1449","1449 - Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Jahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Everything has a purification, and the purification of the body is fasting."
"1450","1450 - Abd al-Rahim ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Muharibi and Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to me, they said: Zaidah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Sulaym narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Jallas narrate, he said: Marwan asked Abu Hurayrah: How did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray over the funeral? He said: He would say: O Allah, You created it and You guided it to Islam, and You took its soul; You know its secret and its open. We have come as intercessors, so forgive it."
"1451","1451 - al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from Uthman ibn Abi Sawdah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a Muslim visits his brother or visits him for the sake of Allah, Allah Almighty says: You are pure and your walking is pure, and you have taken a dwelling in Paradise."
"1452","1452 - Umar ibn Sad narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mawhab, from his uncle, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you knew what is upon him in passing in front of his brother intercepting him while he converses privately with his Lord, standing in that place for forty years would be dearer to him than the step he took in front of him."
"1453","1453 - Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah al-Rabadhi, from Ayyub ibn Khalid, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come from my community on the Day of Resurrection like the night and the flood. The angels will say, when there comes with Muhammad of his community more than what came with all the prophets: [end]. Note in the printed edition and the manuscript: Ubaydullah, while the sources of takhrij have it as Abdullah, and Allah knows best."
"1454","1454 - Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from his brother, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, none enters Paradise except one who is merciful. We said: All of us are merciful, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Mercy is not that one of you shows mercy to his own kin; rather it is that he shows mercy to the people at large and feels pain for the people at large."
"1455","1455 - Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Tahla, from Mihsan ibn Ali, from Awf ibn al-Harith, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution and perfects his ablution, then sets out and finds that the people have already prayed, Allah will give him the reward of one who prayed it and attended it, without decreasing anything from their reward."
"1456","1456 - Qabisah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from al-Tufawi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The perfume of women is that whose color is apparent and whose scent is hidden, and the perfume of men is that whose scent is apparent and whose color is hidden."
"1457","1457 - Said ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu al-Dahhak, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Indeed in Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider travels a hundred years, or seventy years. Shubah said: And I think only a hundred years. Then he said: A hundred years without crossing it - the tree of eternity."
"1458","1458 - Abu Ali al-Hanafi informed me, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mihran, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The farther then the farther from the mosques, the greater in reward."
"1459","1459 - Abu Ali al-Hanafi narrated to me, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn al-Ala ibn Jariyah al-Thaqafi, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: From the time one of you leaves his house toward my mosque, one foot writes a good deed and the other erases an evil deed."
"1460","1460 - Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Abu Aqil al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Sinan al-Tamimi narrated to us, he said: I heard Bukayr ibn Fayruz, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fears sets out at night, and whoever sets out at night reaches the destination. Verily the merchandise of Allah is precious; verily the merchandise of Allah is Paradise."
"1461","1461 - Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Ubayd ibn Abi Ubayd, the freedman of Abu Ruhm, he said: I was walking with Abu Hurayrah when a woman passed by with her scent wafting. He said to her: O maidservant of the Almighty, where are you going, or where do you intend? She said: To the mosque. He said: Did you perfume yourself for it? She said: Yes. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any woman who perfumes herself for this mosque - she does not perfume herself except for prayer in it - her prayer will not be accepted until she bathes her bath from major impurity."
"1462","1462 - Abu al-Walid narrated to me, he said: Abu Awanah informed us, from Yala ibn Ata, from Abu Alqamah al-Ansari, he said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to me from his mouth to my mouth, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah. And whoever obeys the ruler has obeyed me. The ruler is only a shield. If he prays sitting, pray sitting. When he says: Allah hears him who praises Him, say: O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise. For when the speech of the people of earth coincides with the speech of the people of heaven, he is forgiven what has passed of his sin. He said: And Caesar will perish and there will be no Caesar after him, and Khosrow will perish and there will be no Khosrow after him. He said: And he said: Seek refuge in Allah from five: from the punishment of Hell and the punishment of the grave and the trial of life and death and the trial of the False Messiah."
"1463","1463 - Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Abu Harun al-Abdi narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that dogs are a community among communities, I would have ordered their killing; so kill of them every jet-black one. He said: So I said to Abu Hurayrah: What is it with their black ones as against their red ones? Abu Hurayrah said: I said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as you said, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Blessed and Exalted cursed a tribe of the jinn and transformed them into beasts on earth; these black dogs are of the jinn and they are wicked of prey."
"1464","1464 - Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Numan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Hayyan, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Love of these four does not gather except in the heart of a believer: Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman and Ali."
"1465","1465 - Umar ibn Said al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Ubaydullah, from Khalid ibn Husayn, from Abu Hurayrah: I never saw anyone who said more often: I seek Allah's forgiveness and turn to Him in repentance, than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1466","1466 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad, who is al-Razi, narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Mujahid, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhubab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child of adultery will not enter Paradise, nor anything of his progeny to seven forefathers."
"1467","1467 - Yamar ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Sulayman, from Zayd ibn Abi Attab, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best house among the Muslims is a house in which there is an orphan who is treated well, and the worst house among the Muslims is a house in which there is an orphan who is treated badly. Then he said with his two fingers: I and the guardian of the orphan are in Paradise like this, while pointing with his two fingers."
"1468","1468 - Yamar narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Ghazwan informed us, from Ibn Abi Num al-Bajali, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Abu al-Qasim, the Prophet of Repentance (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: Whoever slanders an innocent slave with what he said against him, the legal punishment will be carried out upon him on the Day of Resurrection, unless he is as he said. End of the Musnad of Abu Hurayrah."
"1469","1469 - Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Sufyan ibn Husayn informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came down one night in Ramadan and prayed in the mosque, and people prayed behind him. When morning came they mentioned that, and the people grew numerous on the second night. When it was the third night, the mosque was crowded with its people, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not come down to them that night. When morning came they mentioned that to him, and he said: I knew of your place, and I did that deliberately."
"1470","1470 - Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray eleven rakahs at night; when dawn broke, he would pray two light rakahs, then recline on his right side until the caller to prayer came and informed him of the prayer."
"1471","1471 - Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: A group of Jews entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Death be upon you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And upon you. Aishah said: So I understood it and said: Upon you be death and curse. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gently, O Aishah; indeed Allah loves gentleness in every matter. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not hear what they said? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did I not say: Upon you?"
"1472","1472 - Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would seek refuge from sin and debt. Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: O Messenger of Allah, how often you seek refuge from debt? He said: When one is in debt and promises, he breaks his promise, and when he speaks, he lies."
"1473","1473 - Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: A woman came with two daughters asking me, and she found nothing with me except a single date. I gave it to her, and she split it between her two daughters and ate nothing of it. Then she stood and left, she and her two daughters. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me shortly after that, and I told him her story. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is tested with something of these daughters and treats them well, they will be a shield for him from the Fire."
"1474","1474 - Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would blow upon himself with the refuge-seeking surahs. He said: So I asked al-Zuhri: How would he blow upon himself? He said: He would blow upon his hands, then wipe his face with them. She said: When he became heavy (with illness), I began to blow upon him with them and wipe him with his own hand (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1475","1475 - Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not marry over Khadijah until she died."
"1476","1476 - Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the voice of Abu Musa while he was reciting, and said: This one has been given of the flutes of the family of Dawud."
"1477","1477 - Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: Prayer was obligated upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Makkah two rakahs, two rakahs. When he went out to Madinah, it was obligated as four, while the travel prayer was left as two rakahs. al-Zuhri said: So I said to Urwah: What led Aishah to complete the prayer while traveling, though she knew that Allah Almighty only obligated it as two rakahs? He said: She interpreted of that what Uthman interpreted of completing the prayer at Mina."
"1478","1478 - Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would leave an act though he loved to do it, fearing that the people would follow it as sunnah and it would be obligated upon them. She said: And he loved what was light upon the people."
"1479","1479 - Abd al-Razzaq informed me, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels were created from light, the jinn were created from a smokeless flame of fire, and Adam was created from what has been described to you."
"1480","1480 - Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: This is Jibril, and he conveys peace to you. She said: And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. You see what we do not see."
"1481","1481 - Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never struck a servant with his hand, nor a woman, nor anything, except that he strove in the cause of Allah. Nor did he avenge himself for anything done to him until the sanctities of Allah were violated, then he would avenge for Allah Almighty. Nor was he given choice between two matters except that he chose the easier of them, unless it was a sin; if it was a sin, he was the farthest of people from sin."
"1482","1482 - Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah and Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: A man asked Aishah: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) work in his house? She said: Yes, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would mend his sandal and sew his garment and work in his house as one of you works in his house."
"1483","Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Burqan narrated to us, saying: I asked al-Zuhri about a man who gives his wife the choice and she chooses him, and he said: Urwa narrated to me, from A'isha, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and said: I shall present a matter to you, and you need not hasten until you consult your parents. I said: What is this matter? She said: Then he recited to me: O Prophet, say to your wives: If you desire the life of this world and its adornment, come, I shall provide for you and release you with a fair release. And if you desire Allah and His Messenger and the Last Abode, then Allah has prepared for the doers of good among you a great reward. A'isha said: So I said to him: In which of this do you command me to consult my parents? Rather, I desire Allah and His Messenger and the Last Abode. A'isha said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was pleased with that and it delighted him, and he said: I shall present to your companions what I presented to you. I said: Then do not inform them of what I chose, but he did not do so; he would say to them as he had said to A'isha, then he would say: A'isha has chosen Allah and His Messenger and the Last Abode. A'isha said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had given us the choice, and he did not intend that as a divorce."
"1484","Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to me, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwa, from A'isha, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to sleep, he would join his hands and blow into them and recite: Say, He is Allah, the One, and Say, I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak, and Say, I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind, then he would wipe with them over his face and his head and the rest of his body. Uqayl said: And I saw Ibn Shihab doing that."
"1485","Uthman ibn Umar informed us, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from A'isha, that al-Hawla passed by her while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with her. She said: So I said: This is al-Hawla, and they claim that she does not sleep at night. He said: She does not sleep at night? Take of deeds what you are able to bear; for by Allah, Allah does not tire until you tire."
"1486","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Mu'ammal, a man of the people of Sham, who said: I heard al-Zuhri narrating from Urwa, from A'isha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he had prayed two rak'ahs before Fajr, would lie down."
"1487","Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to me, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwa, from A'isha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the believer falls ill, that purifies him just as the bellows purify the dross of iron."
"1488","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, from A'isha, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had finished with al-Ahzab, he entered the washroom and bathed, then Jibril (peace be upon him) came to him. She said: So I saw him through the opening of the house with dust binding his head, and he said: O Muhammad, you have laid down your arms? Jibril said: We have not laid down our arms yet; rise against Banu Qurayza."
"1489","Abu Usama informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from A'isha, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to love sweets and honey."
"1490","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Ma'mar, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from A'isha, who said: Al-Harith ibn Hisham asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, how does the revelation come to you? He said: It comes to me sometimes with a ringing like the ringing of a bell, then it parts from me while I have retained it, and it is the hardest upon me; and sometimes it comes to me in the form of the angel - or he said: the man - and speaks to me, and I retain what he says."
"1491","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from A'isha, who said: A month would pass upon us in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which we would kindle no fire, and it was only water and dates, except that may Allah reward some women of the Ansar with good, for they would sometimes gift us some milk."
"1492","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from A'isha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the trial of the Fire and the punishment of the Fire, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of the trial of poverty and from the evil of the trial of riches, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the False Messiah. O Allah, purify my heart of my sins as You purified the white garment of filth, and distance between me and my sins as You distanced between the east and the west. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness and old age and sin and debt."
"1493","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from A'isha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gentleness was never in a people but it benefited them, and harshness was never in a people but it harmed them."
"1494","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from A'isha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray sitting, then when he was near his bowing he would stand and recite thirty or forty verses, then bow."
"1495","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, who said: Abu Bakr asked A'isha: In how many garments was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shrouded? She said: In three garments. He said: And shroud me in three garments: my garment along with two other garments, and wash it - his garment which he used to wear. A'isha said: Shall we not buy a new one for you? He said: No, the living are more in need of the new; it is only for the discharge, meaning what comes out of him. Then he said: On which day did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) die? She said: On Monday. He said: Which day is this? She said: Monday. He said: I hope to remain until the night. Then he died in the evening and was buried that night before morning, may Allah be pleased with him."
"1496","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Sufyan, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wishes, let him wish abundantly, for he is only asking his Lord, Almighty and Exalted."
"1497","Muhadir narrated to me, Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform ruqya: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind; in Your hand is healing; none removes it but You."
"1498","Muhadir narrated to me, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with water."
"1499","Khalid ibn Makhlad al-Bajali narrated to me, Yahya ibn Umayr narrated to me, Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to me, from his father, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a camel from a Bedouin for a wasq of ajwa dates, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought dates with his family but did not find them, so he mentioned that to the Bedouin, and the Bedouin shouted: O treachery! The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather you, O enemy of Allah, are the treacherous one. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him, for the holder of a right has a say. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Khawla bint Hakim and sent the Bedouin with the messenger, saying: Say to her: I bought this camel from this Bedouin for a wasq of dates, but I did not find it with my family, so lend me a wasq of ajwa dates for this Bedouin. When the Bedouin received his due, he returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said to him: Have you received? He said: Yes, and you fulfilled and gave in good manner. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people are those who fulfill and give in good manner."
"1500","Abdullah ibn Maslama narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from A'isha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A servant may do the deeds of the people of Paradise while he is of the people of the Fire, and a servant may do the deeds of the people of the Fire while he is of the people of Paradise."
"1501","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from A'isha, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss while fasting, then she laughed."
"1502","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, from A'isha, that some people were worshipping with severe worship, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, we are not like you, for Allah has forgiven you your sins, past and future. He said: By Allah, I am the most knowledgeable of you about Allah and the most fearful of Him among you. And he said: Upon you is of deeds what you are able to bear, for Allah, Almighty and Exalted, does not tire until you tire. And the most beloved deed to him was the continuous one, even if little."
"1503","Shaddad ibn Hakim narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would accept the gift and reward for it."
"1504","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, Abu Usama narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from A'isha, that she borrowed a necklace from Asma and it was lost, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent some of his companions to seek it, and prayer overtook them. She said: So they prayed without ablution, and when they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) they complained of that to him. She said: Then the verse of tayammum was revealed, and Usayd ibn Hudayr said: May Allah reward you with good, for by Allah no matter ever befell you but Allah made for you a way out of it and made therein a blessing for the Muslims."
"1505","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from A'isha, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never left the two rak'ahs after Asr in my house."
"1506","Al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from his father, from A'isha, who said: The bed of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was of leather stuffed with palm fiber."
"1507","Al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, Hisham ibn Urwa informed us, from his father, from A'isha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three white Yemeni garments of cotton."
"1508","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayya, from Abdullah ibn Urwa, from Urwa, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me in Shawwal and I was brought to him in Shawwal, so which of his wives was more favored with him than me? He said: And she liked to bring her women in in Shawwal."
"1509","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Urwa, from A'isha, who said: I missed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night, so I went out and there he was at al-Baqi', raising his head to the sky. He said: O A'isha, did you fear that Allah and His Messenger would wrong you? She said: I said: It is not that, O Messenger of Allah, but I thought you had gone to some of your wives. He said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, descends to the lowest heaven on the night of the middle of Sha'ban and forgives more than the number of the hairs of the sheep of Kalb."
"1510","Ja'far ibn Awn informed us, Hisham ibn Sa'd informed us, from Abu Hazim, from Yazid ibn Ruman, from Urwa, from A'isha, who said: A'isha said to me: O son of my sister, by Allah, we would look at the crescent, then the crescent, then the crescent, three crescents in two months, and no fire was kindled in the houses of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: O aunt, what sustained you? She said: We had neighbors from the Ansar, good neighbors they were; they had milk-animals, and they would send to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of their milk, and he would mix it for us and give us to drink."
"1511","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Urwa, from A'isha, that a man came and sought permission upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What an evil brother of the people and son of the tribe is this. When he entered, he turned to him with his face and conversed with him, and when he left, A'isha said: O Messenger of Allah, you said about him what you said, then you turned to him with your face and your speech. He said: Among the worst of people in station with Allah on the Day of Resurrection is a man whom people avoid because of his evil - or he said: because of his obscenity."
"1512","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abi Farwa, from Uthman ibn Urwa, from his father, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed, that is an expiation for every sin short of polytheism."
"1513","Qabisa ibn Uqba narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Usama ibn Zayd, from Uthman ibn Urwa, from Urwa, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Almighty and Exalted, and His angels send blessings upon those who join the rows."
"1514","Ibrahim ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Tamim ibn Salama, from Urwa, from A'isha, who said: Blessed is He whose hearing encompasses all sounds. A woman would confide to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I heard some of her speech and some was hidden from me, when Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: Allah has heard the saying of her who disputes with you concerning her husband."
"1515","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Shu'ba ibn al-Hajjaj informed us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salama, from A'isha, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which deeds are best. He said: The most constant, even if little."
"1516","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salama, that he asked A'isha about the fasting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she said: He would fast until we said: He does not break his fast, and he would break his fast until we said: He does not fast. And I never saw him fasting more in a month than in Sha'ban; he would fast all of Sha'ban except a little - rather, he would fast all of Sha'ban."
"1517","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salama, from A'isha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at the moon and said: O A'isha, seek refuge with Allah from the evil of this, for this is the darkening night when it settles."
"1518","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Salih ibn Muhammad, from Abu Salama, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not raise his head to the sky except that he said: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your obedience."
"1519","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Musa ibn Ubayda, from Maslama ibn Abi al-Ash'ath, from Abu Salih, from Abu Salama, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Jibril: I wished to see you in your form. He said: Do you love that? He said: Yes. He said: Your appointment is such-and-such of the night at Baqi' al-Gharqad. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met him at his appointment, and he spread a wing of his wings and blocked the horizon of the sky until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw nothing of the sky, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell unconscious at that."
"1520","Amr ibn Awn informed me, Abu Awana informed us, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, from his father, who said: A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: I was accused of that with which I was accused while I was heedless, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting with me, when revelation was sent down to him. She said: And when revelation was sent down to him, something like slumber would seize him. So revelation was sent down to him while he was sitting with me, then he sat upright and wiped his face, then said: O A'isha, rejoice. I said: By the praise of Allah, not by your praise. Then he recited this verse: Indeed those who accuse chaste, heedless, believing women, to the end of the two verses."
"1521","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama, from A'isha and Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained in Makkah ten years with the Qur'an descending upon him, and in Madinah ten years."
"1522","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub, who said: Uqayl and Yunus narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salama, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of my nation bears a debt, then strives to repay it and dies before repaying it, I am his guardian."
"1523","Abu Asim informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Qasim, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to A'isha: Whoever is given his share of gentleness is given his share of provision, and whoever is denied his share of gentleness is denied his share of provision."
"1524","Uthman ibn Umar informed us, Shu'ba informed us, from Waqid, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from A'isha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever pleases Allah at the displeasure of people, Allah suffices him against people; and whoever angers Allah to please people, Allah entrusts him to people."
"1525","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from al-Qasim, from A'isha, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw rain, he would say: O Allah, a heavy downpour - or he said: a wholesome, beneficial rain."
"1526","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from al-Thawri, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah ibn Asim, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from A'isha, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enter upon Uthman ibn Maz'un while he was dead, and he uncovered his face, then bent over him and kissed him, then wept until I saw tears flowing upon his cheeks."
"1527","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Hayyan, from Ibn Bujayd, from his grandmother, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not turn away the beggar, even with a hoof."
"1528","Ibrahim ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us, al-Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, Baqiyya ibn al-Walid informed us, Bahir ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Kathir ibn Murra al-Hadrami, from A'isha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her with Abu Bakr, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: O A'isha, feed us. She said: By Allah, we have no food. He said: Feed us. She said: By Allah, we have no food. He said: Feed us. She said: By Allah, we have no food. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, a believing woman does not swear about a thing that it is not with her while it is with her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And how do you know whether she is a believer or not? The example of the believing woman among women is like the white-footed crow among crows. And the Fire was created from the foolish, and women are of the foolish except the possessor of justice and the lamp."
"1529","Ibrahim ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us, al-Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Farwa ibn Nawfal, who said: I said to A'isha: Teach me something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would supplicate with, that I might supplicate with it. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, forgive me what I know and what I do not know."
"1530","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from al-Hasan, from Sa'sa'a, from al-Ahnaf, who said: A woman entered upon A'isha with her two daughters, so she gave her three dates; she gave each of them a date, then split the remaining one between them. He said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to her and she told him. He said: What amazed you? She has entered Paradise through it."
"1531","Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salama, from Umm Salama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me after Asr and prayed two rak'ahs. I said: O Messenger of Allah, this prayer you did not used to pray. He said: A delegation of Banu Tamim came and kept me from two rak'ahs which I used to pray after Zuhr."
"1532","Ya'la narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Nafi', from Safiyya, from A'isha and Umm Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person for more than three days, except over her husband. And mourning is: that she does not comb, nor apply kohl, nor touch perfume, nor dye, nor wear a dyed garment, nor leave her house."
"1533","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Abdullah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind informed us, from his father, who said: Umm Salama said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sleeping in my house when Husayn came toddling. She said: So I sat at the door and held him back, fearing he would enter and wake him. She said: Then I was heedless of something, so he crawled and entered and sat upon his stomach. She said: Then I heard the weeping of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I came and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah I did not know of him. He said: Jibril (peace be upon him) came to me while he was sitting upon my stomach, and said to me: Do you love him? I said: Yes. He said: Your nation shall kill him. Shall I not show you the soil in which he shall be killed? He said: I said: Yes. He said: Then he struck with his wing and brought me this soil. She said: And there was in his hand red soil, while he wept and said: Would that I knew who shall kill you after me."
"1534","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to me, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, saying: I heard Umm Salama narrating that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would often say in his supplication: O Allah, Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. I said: O Messenger of Allah, are hearts indeed turned? He said: Yes; there is no created being of Allah of the children of Adam but his heart is between two fingers of the fingers of Allah; if He wills He keeps it straight, and if He wills He turns it aside. So we ask Allah our Lord not to turn our hearts aside after He guided us, and we ask Him to grant us mercy from Himself, for He is the Bestower. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not teach me a supplication with which I may supplicate for myself? He said: Yes; say: O Allah, Lord of the Prophet Muhammad, forgive my sin and remove the anger of my heart and protect me from the misleading trials as they befall us."
"1535","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi A'isha, who said: I heard a freedman of Umm Salama narrating from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when morning came he would say: O Allah, I ask You for beneficial knowledge and wholesome provision and accepted deeds."
"1536","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Sha'bi, from Umm Salama, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left his house, he would say: In the name of Allah; my Lord, I seek refuge in You from slipping or straying, or wronging or being ignorant, or being treated ignorantly."
"1537","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq, from Umm Salama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you attend the dead, speak good, for the angels say amen to what you say. She said: So when Abu Salama died, I said: O Messenger of Allah, what shall I say? He said: Say: O Allah, forgive him and grant us after him a good successor. So Allah granted me after him Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1538","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, Isra'il informed us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abu Salama, from Umm Salama, who said: I never saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fast a complete month except Sha'ban, for he would join it with Ramadan so they would be two consecutive months. And he would fast of the year until we said: He does not break his fast, and he would break his fast until we said: He does not fast."
"1539","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Umm Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: My Lord, forgive and have mercy and guide me to the straightest path."
"1540","Zayd ibn al-Hubab al-Ukli informed us, Abd al-Mu'min ibn Khalid al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Burayda narrated to me, from Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There was no garment more beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than the shirt."
"1541","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, Muhammad ibn al-Fudayl narrated to us, from Abu Nasr Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Musawir al-Himyari, from his mother, from Umm Salama, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Any woman who dies while her husband is pleased with her shall enter Paradise."
"1542","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Hammam, from Qatada, from Salih Abu al-Khalil, from Safina, from Umm Salama, that during the illness in which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, he would say: The prayer and what your right hands possess. He kept saying it until his tongue overflowed with it."
"1543","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Huraym, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Abu Kathir, freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Say at the call to Maghrib: O Allah, at the coming of Your night and the passing of Your day and the voices of Your supplications and the presence of Your prayers, forgive me. And when she awoke at night she would say: My Lord, forgive me and have mercy and guide to the straightest path."
"1544","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdala, from Sawa al-Khuza'i, from Hafsa, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast three days of the month: Monday and Thursday, and Monday of the next week."
"1545","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'ida, from Asim, from al-Musayyab - and another besides Husayn said: from Za'ida, from Sawa, from Hafsa - who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took his bed, he would place his right hand under his right cheek. And his right was for his food and drink and purification and clothes and prayer, and his left was for other than that. And he would fast Monday and Thursday."
"1546","Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Hafsa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would lighten the two rak'ahs before Fajr."
"1547","Abu Asim informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Uthman ibn Khalid, from Abdullah ibn Sa'id, that Hafsa informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had placed his garment between his thighs, then Abu Bakr came and entered while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in that state, then Umar came, then Ali came, then people of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and conversed with him. Then Uthman came and sought permission, so he covered himself with it, then permitted him. When they left, I said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr sought permission, then Umar, then Ali, while you were in your state, but when Uthman sought permission you covered yourself with the garment. He said: Shall I not be shy before one before whom the angels are shy?"
"1548","Ya'la ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Maymuna, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I freed a slave girl of mine, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me and I informed him of freeing her. He said: May Allah reward you; had you given her to your maternal uncles, it would have been greater for your reward."
"1549","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, Jarir al-Razi narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ziyad ibn Amr ibn Hind, from Imran ibn Hudhayfa, who said: Maymuna would take debts frequently, so her family spoke to her about that and blamed her and turned upon her. She said: I shall not leave debt, for I heard my Prophet and my beloved (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no one who takes a debt while Allah, Almighty and Exalted, knows that he intends to repay it, but Allah, Almighty and Exalted, repays it for him in this world."
"1550","Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I asked Maymuna, my maternal aunt, about the washing of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from major impurity. She said: A vessel would be brought, and he would pour with his right upon his left and wash his private parts and what had touched him, then perform ablution as for prayer, then wash his head and the rest of his body, then move and wash his feet. Then a towel would be brought and placed before him, and he would shake his fingers and not touch it."
"1551","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Maymuna, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of us was menstruating, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would command her to wrap herself, then he would touch her."
"1552","Al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, Isra'il ibn Yunus informed us, Abu Ishaq informed us, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Anbasa ibn Abi Sufyan, from his sister Umm Habiba, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays twelve voluntary rak'ahs, a house shall be built for him in Paradise: four before Zuhr, two after Zuhr, two after Maghrib, two after Isha, and two before the Fajr prayer."
"1553","Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Hassan ibn Atiyya, who said: When death descended upon Anbasa ibn Abi Sufyan, his distress intensified, so it was said: What is this distress? He said: I heard Umm Habiba - meaning his sister - saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, Allah, Almighty and Exalted, forbids his flesh to the Fire. And I have not left them since."
"1554","Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Khunays narrated to me, Sa'id ibn Hassan al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Umm Salih narrated to me, from Safiyya bint Shayba, from Umm Habiba, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The speech of the son of Adam is against him, not for him, except enjoining good or forbidding evil or remembrance of Allah, Almighty and Exalted."
"1555","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Suwayd ibn Qays, from Mu'awiya ibn Hudayj, from Mu'awiya ibn Abi Sufyan, may Allah be pleased with him, that he asked his sister Umm Habiba, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whether the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray in the garment in which he had intercourse. She said: Yes, if he saw no harm in it."
"1556","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Safiyya bint Huyayy, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in retreat, so I came to visit him at night and spoke with him, then I rose to return, so he rose with me to return me. She said: And her dwelling was in the house of Usama ibn Zayd. Two men of the Ansar passed, and when they saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) they hastened. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: At your ease; she is Safiyya bint Huyayy. They said: Glory be to Allah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Satan flows in man like blood, and I feared he would cast evil - or he said: something - into your hearts."
"1557","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Shu'ba informed us, from Qatada, from Abu Ayyub, from Juwayriya bint al-Harith, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me on Friday while I was fasting, and said: Did you fast yesterday? I said: No. He said: Will you fast tomorrow? I said: No. He said: Then break your fast."
"1558","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from his maternal aunt Umm Uthman, from al-Tufayl, nephew of Juwayriya, from Juwayriya, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever wears a garment of silk in this world, Allah shall clothe him with a garment of fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"1559","Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jubayr, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Umm Sharik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded killing the gecko, and said: It would blow upon Ibrahim (peace be upon him)."
"1560","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Husayn, from his grandmother Umm Husayn, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressing the people at Mina, wrapped in his garment, while the muscle of his upper arm trembled, saying: O people, fear Allah and hear and obey, even if an Abyssinian slave is placed in authority over you; hear him and obey him as long as he upholds the Book of Allah for you."
"1561","Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, Yahya ibn Husayn narrated to us, informing me that he heard his grandmother saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressing at Arafat, saying: Even if a slave is appointed over you to lead you by the Book of Allah, hear him and obey him."
"1562","Zayd ibn Hubab al-Ukli narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubayda al-Rabadhi, Mundhir ibn al-Jahm narrated to me, from Umar ibn Khalda al-Ansari, from his mother, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Ali on the days of Mina to proclaim: These are days of eating and drinking and intercourse."
"1563","Abdullah ibn Maslama narrated to me, Fa'id narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi', from his grandmother, who said: When a wound or injury befell the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I would place henna upon it."
"1564","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from a woman called Umm al-Ala, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited her in her illness and said: Rejoice, O Umm al-Ala, for the illness of the Muslim removes his sins as fire removes the dross of silver and gold."
"1565","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, Sharik narrated to us, from Khalaf ibn Hawshab, from Maymun, who said: I asked Umm al-Darda: Did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The first thing placed in the Scale is good character."
"1566","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Umm Ghurab, from a woman called Aqila, from Salama, sister of Kharasha ibn al-Hurr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There shall come upon people a time when they stand for an hour and find no imam to lead them in prayer."
"1567","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Sulayman ibn Amr ibn al-Ahwas, from his mother Umm Jundub, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoning the Aqaba pillar from the belly of the valley on the Day of Sacrifice while upon his mount, then he left, and a woman of Khath'am followed him with a boy of hers afflicted with an ailment. She said: O Messenger of Allah, this is my son and the remainder of my family, and he has an ailment; he does not speak. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me some water. Water was brought, so he washed his hands and rinsed his mouth, then gave it to her and said: Give him to drink of it and pour upon him, and seek healing from Allah, Almighty and Exalted, for him. He said: Then I met the woman and said: Would you grant me some of it? She said: It is only for this afflicted one. He said: Then I met the woman the next year and asked her about the boy, and she said: He recovered and became intelligent with an intelligence unlike the minds of men."
"1568","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shu'ba informed us, from Habib, who said: I heard a freedwoman of ours called Layla narrating from Umm Umara, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought food and ate of it, then said to her: Come near and eat. She said: I am fasting. He said: When food is eaten in the presence of the fasting person, the angels send blessings upon him until they finish."
"1569","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Ghannam, from some of his family, from Umm Farwa - and she was of those who pledged to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which deed is best. He said: Prayer at the beginning of its time."
"1570","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Hani ibn Uthman narrated to us, from his mother Humayda bint Yasir, from her grandmother Yusayra - and she was of the emigrant women - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Upon you is tahlil and tasbih and taqdis; do not be heedless lest you forget mercy. And count with the fingertips, for they shall be questioned and made to speak."
"1571","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from al-Harith ibn Fudayl, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Ka'b, from his father, who said: When death came to Ka'b, Umm Bishr bint al-Bara came to him and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, if you meet my son so-and-so, convey my greeting to him. He said to her: May Allah forgive you, O Umm Bishr, we are busier than that. She said: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The soul of the believer roams in Paradise wherever it wills, and the soul of the disbeliever is in Sijjin? He said: Yes. She said: Then it is that."
"1572","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, saying: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from Umm Mubashshir al-Ansariyya, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I was in a palm-grove of mine, and said: To whom do these palms belong? I said: To me. He said: Who planted them, a Muslim or a disbeliever? I said: A Muslim. He said: No Muslim plants a planting or sows a crop from which a man or a bird or a beast eats, but it is charity for him."
"1573","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar and al-Thawri informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, who said: We slaughtered a horse in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ate it."
"1574","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, saying: I heard Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, who said: We broke our fast in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Ramadan one day, then the sun appeared. A man said to Hisham: Did they make it up or not? He said: I do not know."
"1575","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwa, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that when she made tharid, she would cover it somewhat until its heat departed, then say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is greater for blessing."
"1576","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Abu Umar, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that she brought out a cloak buttoned with brocade, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wear this when he met the enemy."
"1577","Habban ibn Hilal and Sulayman ibn Harb and Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to me, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah; Allah forgives all sins - and He does not care."
"1578","Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Greatest Name of Allah is in these two verses: Allah, there is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer, and: Your god is one God."
"1579","Abu Asim informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever defends the flesh of his brother in his absence, it is due upon Allah to free him from the Fire."
"1580","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of your best? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Those when seen, Allah is remembered. Then he said: Shall I not inform you of your worst: those who carry tales, who corrupt between loved ones, who seek hardship for the innocent."
"1581","Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'ida, from Aban ibn Abi Ayyash, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Almighty and Exalted, shall raise on the Day of Resurrection a caller who calls: The people of the gathering shall know today who is most worthy of honor. Where are those whom neither trade nor sale distracts from the remembrance of Allah? So they rise and enter Paradise. Then the caller returns and says: The people of the gathering shall know who is most worthy of honor: Where are those whose sides forsake their beds? So they enter Paradise. Then the caller returns and says: The people of the gathering shall know who is most worthy of honor, saying: Where are those who praise Allah in every state? And they are more numerous than the first two groups, so they enter Paradise."
"1582","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The False Messiah shall remain in the earth forty years, with a year like a month, a month like a week, a week like a day, and a day like the blazing of a palm-frond in fire."
"1583","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to me, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me, Asma bint Yazid narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses have good tied in their forelocks forever until the Day of Resurrection. Whoever ties them as preparation in the path of Allah and spends upon them seeking reward in the path of Allah, then their satiety and hunger, their quenching and thirst, their dung and urine are success in his scales on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever ties them for show and repute and pride and boasting, then their satiety and hunger and thirst and quenching and dung and urine are loss in his scales on the Day of Resurrection."
"1584","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Jahm al-Adawi, who said: I heard Fatima bint Qays saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: When you become lawful, inform me. So she informed him. He said: Then Mu'awiya and Abu Jahm ibn Mukhayyir and Usama ibn Zayd proposed to her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for Mu'awiya, he is a poor man with no wealth; and as for Abu Jahm, he is a man who beats women; but Usama ibn Zayd - so she said with her hand like this: Usama, Usama? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Obedience to Allah and obedience to His Messenger are better for you. So she married him and was envied for it."
"1585","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from his mother Umm al-Fadl, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting al-Mursalat in Maghrib."
"1586","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Tammam ibn al-Abbas, who said: Umm al-Fadl heard me reciting: By those sent forth in succession, and said: O my son, this is the last surah I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting, leading the people in the Maghrib prayer."
"1587","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Aswad narrated to me, from al-Nu'man ibn Abi Ayyash al-Zuraqi, from Khawla bint Thamir al-Ansariyya, that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The world is green and sweet, and men shall plunge into the wealth of Allah without right; for them is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"1588","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah, from Ubayd Sanuta, from Khawla bint Qays, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This wealth is sweet and green; whoever takes it rightfully, it shall be blessed for him therein. And many a plunger into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger shall have the Fire on the day he meets Him."
"1589","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Dhakwan Abu al-Husayn, who said: Women would beat the tambourines, so I mentioned that to al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh, and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me on the day of my wedding and sat at the place of this bed of mine, while with us were two slave girls beating the tambourine and eulogizing my fathers who were killed on the day of Badr. They said in what they said - so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for this, do not say it."
"1590","Abu Asim narrated to us, from Yasar ibn Abd al-Malik, who said: My grandmother Umm Hakim bint Dinar, freedwoman of Umm Ishaq, narrated to me, from Umm Ishaq, who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and bread and meat were brought. She said: And I desired to eat of the food of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Come, O Umm Ishaq, and eat. She said: So I ate, then he handed me a bone with meat, so I raised it to my mouth, then I remembered that I was fasting, so my hand remained, unable to raise it to my mouth nor to put it down. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is with you, O Umm Ishaq? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I was fasting. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Complete your fast. Then Dhu al-Yadayn said: Now, after she is full? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is only provision which Allah drove to her."
"1591","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Hathma, from al-Shifa bint Abdullah - and she was of the emigrant women - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the best deed. He said: Faith in Allah, and striving in the path of Allah, and an accepted pilgrimage."
"1592","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his mother Umm Kulthum bint Uqba - and she was of the first emigrant women - who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: He is not a liar who reconciles between people, saying good or conveying good."
"1593","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Kharija ibn Zayd, who said: Umm al-Ala al-Ansariyya, when the emigrants came to Madinah, the Ansar cast lots for their lodging. She said: So Uthman ibn Maz'un fell to us. He fell ill, so we nursed him, then he died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and entered upon him, so I said: May the mercy of Allah be upon you, O Abu al-Sa'ib; my testimony is that Allah has honored you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And how do you know that Allah has honored him? I said: I do not know, by Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for him, certainty has come to him from his Lord, Almighty and Exalted, and I hope for him good from Allah, Almighty and Exalted. By Allah, I do not know, though I am the Messenger of Allah, what shall be done with me, nor with you. She said: So I said: By Allah, I shall never declare anyone pure after him. She said: Then I saw for Uthman afterwards in a dream a flowing spring, so I related it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: That is his deed. Ma'mar said: And I heard another besides al-Zuhri saying: The Muslims disliked what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Uthman, until Zaynab bint Rasulillah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, and he said: Join our predecessor, Uthman ibn Maz'un."
"1594","Umar ibn Sa'id al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Tunukhi narrated to us, from Makhul, from Umm Ayman, that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advising some of his family, saying: Do not associate anything with Allah, even if you are cut or burned with fire. Do not flee on the day of battle; if death befalls people while you are among them, stand firm. Obey your parents, even if they command you to leave your wealth. Do not abandon prayer deliberately, for whoever abandons prayer deliberately is free of the protection of Allah. Beware of wine, for it is the key to every evil. Beware of disobedience, for it angers Allah. Do not dispute authority with its people, even if you see that it is yours. Spend upon your family of your means, do not lift your stick from them, and make them fear Allah, Almighty and Exalted. Amr said: Another besides Sa'id narrated to us that al-Zuhri said: The one advised with this counsel was Thawban."
